      "name": "DestroyNetworkContext",
      "signature": "void DestroyNetworkContext(void * pContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Destroys a network context and releases all associated resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate context pointer is non-null\n2. If network state (+0x110) exists and thread handle (+0x24) is valid:\n   a. Set shutdown flag (+0x120) to 1\n   b. Enter critical section (+0xc) via Ordinal_10050\n   c. Set close pending flag (+0x2c) to 1\n   d. Leave critical section\n3. Destroy callback queue at offset +0x16c\n4. If network state still valid and thread handle exists:\n   a. Call Ordinal_10005 to close socket and wait for thread\n   b. Clear network state pointer (+0x110)\n5. Call Ordinal_10043 for final cleanup\n\nParameters:\n- pContext (void*): Pointer to network context structure\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x110: Offset to network state pointer\n- 0x120: Shutdown flag offset\n- 0x16c: Callback queue offset\n- 0x24: Thread handle offset in network state\n- 0x2c: Close pending flag in network state\n- 0xc: Critical section offset in network state",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:0efba2de28bd5f233a5dd8d2e8872c6b",
