      "name": "CreateDirectoryRecursive",
      "signature": "int CreateDirectoryRecursive(char * lpszPath)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Recursively creates all directories in the specified path.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input path is non-null and non-empty\n2. Find each backslash separator using Ordinal_571 (strchr)\n3. Copy path prefix up to separator into buffer\n4. Attempt CreateDirectoryA for current component\n5. If fails with ERROR_ALREADY_EXISTS (0xB7) or ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED (5),\n   verify existing entry is a directory via FILE_ATTRIBUTE_DIRECTORY\n6. Continue to next path component until complete\n\nParameters:\n- lpszPath (char*): Full path with backslash separators (e.g., \"C:\\\\Dir1\\\\Dir2\")\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success (all directories created or exist as directories)\n- 0 on failure (null/empty input, path too long, or creation failed)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x5C (92): Backslash character '\\\\'\n- 0x104 (260): MAX_PATH buffer size\n- 0xB7 (183): ERROR_ALREADY_EXISTS\n- 5: ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED\n- 0x10 (16): FILE_ATTRIBUTE_DIRECTORY",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
