      "comment": "Removes an entry from the hash table by key.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if hash table is initialized (offset 0xbd0)\n2. Enter critical section (offset 0x894)\n3. Compute bucket index: dwKey % tableSize (offset 0x8b0)\n4. Walk linked list in bucket looking for matching key\n5. If found, unlink node by updating previous->next pointer\n6. Decrement entry count (offset 0x890)\n7. Leave critical section\n8. Every 2000ms call NullStubProc for periodic cleanup\n\nParameters:\n- this (void*): Hash table object\n- dwKey (uint): Key to remove from hash table\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nStructure Layout:\n| Offset | Type | Description |\n| 0x890 | int | Entry count |\n| 0x894 | CRITICAL_SECTION | Lock |\n| 0x8ac | uint** | Bucket array pointer |\n| 0x8b0 | uint | Bucket count |\n| 0xbd0 | int | Initialized flag |\n\nNode Layout (16 bytes):\n| Offset | Type | Description |\n| 0x0 | uint | Key |\n| 0xc | node* | Next pointer |\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7d0 (2000): Cleanup interval in milliseconds",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
