      "name": "DisconnectClientById",
      "signature": "void DisconnectClientById(void * pServer, dword dwClientId)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Disconnects a client by its unique client ID.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate hash bucket index from client ID using mask at pServer+0xC\n2. Enter critical section for hash bucket (stride 0x18)\n3. Search linked list for client with matching ID\n4. Leave critical section and return if client not found\n5. Return if client already marked for removal (pClient[3] != 0)\n6. Mark client as pending removal (pClient[3] = 1)\n7. Close socket via Ordinal_10000, set handle to -1\n8. Decrement reference count; if non-zero, exit early\n9. Re-acquire bucket lock, unlink client from hash table\n10. Decrement global client count (pServer+0x880)\n11. Unlink from IP-based tracking list at pServer+0x20\n12. Call FUN_6ff66000 to cleanup IP tracking entry\n13. Call DestroyClientContext to free client structure\n\nParameters:\n- pServer (void*): Server context structure containing:\n  - +0x0C: Hash mask for bucket calculation\n  - +0x14: Client hash table array\n  - +0x1C: Critical section array (stride 0x18)\n  - +0x20: IP-based client list array\n  - +0x28: IP list critical section\n  - +0x854: Global client list critical section\n  - +0x880: Active client count\n  - +0xBC8: Optional callback function pointer\n- dwClientId (dword): Unique ID of client to disconnect\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nClient Structure Layout:\n- +0x00: Client ID (matched against dwClientId)\n- +0x04: Next pointer for hash bucket linked list\n- +0x08: Reference count (InterlockedDecrement)\n- +0x0C: Removal flag (0=active, 1=pending removal)\n- +0x10: Socket handle\n- +0x18: IP address (in_addr union)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x18: Critical section array stride (bucket size)\n- 0x854: Offset to global client list critical section\n- 0x880: Offset to active client count\n- 0xBC8: Offset to optional callback",
