      "name": "AsyncDataSetBuffer",
      "signature": "void AsyncDataSetBuffer(void * this, uint dwBuffer, uint dwBufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets new buffer and size for an async data structure, freeing the previous buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert this pointer is non-null\n2. Validate dwFlags magic (0x41737960 masked) matches ASYNC_DATA_VALID\n3. Assert ASYNC_DATA_INUSE flag (bit 0) is set\n4. Free existing buffer at offset 0x3C using pool ID at offset 0x4\n5. Store dwBuffer at offset 0x3C and dwBufferSize at offset 0x40\n\nParameters:\n- this (void*): Pointer to AsyncData structure (ECX, __thiscall)\n- dwBuffer (uint): New buffer address to assign\n- dwBufferSize (uint): Size of the new buffer\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x41737960: ASYNC_DATA_VALID magic (\"Asy`\" ASCII)\n- 0xFFFFFFF0: Mask to extract magic from dwFlags\n- 0x1: ASYNC_DATA_INUSE flag bit\n\nStructure Offsets:\n- 0x04: dwPoolId - Memory pool identifier\n- 0x3C: dwBuffer - Current buffer pointer\n- 0x40: dwBufferSize - Current buffer size\n- 0x48: dwFlags - Validation flags with magic",
