      "name": "QueueClientSendData",
      "signature": "int QueueClientSendData(void * pContext, uint * pClient, byte * pbData, uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Queues data for sending to a client socket with buffering support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter critical section on client connection\n2. Update client timestamp via Ordinal_10055 (GetTickCount)\n3. If no pending data in queue:\n   a. If socket invalid (-1), disconnect and release client\n   b. Call send() directly with data\n   c. If WSAEWOULDBLOCK error, treat as zero bytes sent\n   d. If partial send, queue remaining bytes\n4. If data already queued, append new data to queue\n5. Exit critical section\n\nParameters:\n- pContext (void*): Network context handle\n- pClient (uint*): Client connection structure\n- pbData (byte*): Data buffer to send\n- dwSize (uint): Size of data in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success (data sent or queued)\n- 0 on connection failure (client disconnected)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xB (11): Offset to critical section in client structure\n- 0x1D (29): Offset to send queue head pointer\n- 0x20 (32): Offset to last activity timestamp\n- 0x2733 (10035): WSAEWOULDBLOCK error code\n- 0x421 (1057): Fog memory allocation line number",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
