      "name": "QueueLogEntry",
      "signature": "void QueueLogEntry(char * szSource, char * szMessage, int nLine, int nSeverity, int nFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Queues a log message entry for asynchronous processing by background thread.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if logging system is active (not shutting down, background thread running)\n2. Get message length via Ordinal_506 (strlen)\n3. Allocate log entry structure via FUN_6ff70ec0 (within critical section)\n4. Copy message text and source identifier into entry\n5. Record timestamp via GetLocalTime\n6. Store line number, severity, and flags\n7. Insert entry into doubly-linked list (thread-safe)\n8. Update global counters (entry count and total message bytes)\n\nParameters:\n- szSource (char*): Source identifier string (max 16 chars)\n- szMessage (char*): Log message text\n- nLine (int): Source line number\n- nSeverity (int): Log severity level\n- nFlags (int): Additional flags\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nStructure Layout (Log Entry at offset):\n- 0x00: pNext (linked list next pointer)\n- 0x04: pPrev (linked list prev offset)\n- 0x08: SYSTEMTIME (16 bytes, timestamp)\n- 0x18: szSource[16] (source identifier)\n- 0x28: nType (entry type, set to 1)\n- 0x2C: nLine\n- 0x30: nSeverity\n- 0x34: nFlags\n- 0x38: nMsgLen (message length + 1)\n- 0x3C: szMessage[] (variable length)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
