      "name": "InitAsyncFileOperation",
      "signature": "int * InitAsyncFileOperation(void * pMemPool, uint dwFileHandle, int nAsyncMode, int nFileOffset, int nBufferSize, void * pBuffer, int * pCallback, uint dwUserData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Initializes an async file operation structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocates 0x54 byte AsyncFileOp structure from memory pool\n2. Zeros structure (21 dwords) and sets magic 0x41737960 at offset 0x48\n3. Associates structure with file handle via Ordinal_10102\n4. Sets file offset via Ordinal_10106 if nFileOffset != 0\n5. Gets buffer size from Ordinal_10105 if nBufferSize < 1\n6. If pBuffer NULL: allocates buffer from pool, sets flag bit 2\n7. Else: uses pBuffer directly, clears flag bit 2\n8. Copies 7 dwords from pCallback struct to offset 0x1c if provided\n9. If nAsyncMode and g_fAsyncDataEnabled both set:\n   - Allocates async event, links to structure at offset 0x38\n   - Starts async I/O via Ordinal_10104\n   - Returns structure pointer\n10. Else: Performs sync I/O, invokes callback, CompleteAsyncOperation\n\nParameters:\n- pMemPool (void*): Memory pool for allocations\n- dwFileHandle (uint): File handle to associate with operation\n- nAsyncMode (int): Non-zero enables async operation mode\n- nFileOffset (int): Starting file offset; 0 = no seek\n- nBufferSize (int): Buffer size; <1 uses Ordinal_10105 default\n- pBuffer (void*): User buffer or NULL to auto-allocate\n- pCallback (int*): Callback struct (7 dwords) or NULL\n- dwUserData (uint): User context passed to callbacks\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to AsyncFileOp structure on success\n- NULL on async event allocation failure (cleanup performed)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x54 (84): AsyncFileOp structure size\n- 0x41737960: Magic identifier (structure signature)\n- 0x15 (21): DWORDs to zero (84/4)\n- 0x12d, 0x137, 0x145, 0x187, 0x189: Source line numbers\n\nStructure Layout (offsets):\n- 0x00: File handle (from Ordinal_10102)\n- 0x04: pMemPool pointer\n- 0x08: OVERLAPPED structure start\n- 0x10: nFileOffset\n- 0x18: Event handle copy\n- 0x1c-0x38: Callback struct copy (7 dwords)\n- 0x38: Async event pointer\n- 0x3c: Buffer pointer\n- 0x40: Buffer size\n- 0x44: dwUserData\n- 0x48: Flags (bit 2 = buffer allocated)\n\nFlag Bits (offset 0x48):\n- Bit 1 (0x2): Buffer was allocated internally (needs freeing)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:ceb55c7eed45e1faf6764837503cd14a",
