      "name": "InitializeHeapPage",
      "signature": "int InitializeHeapPage(SbhHeapEntry * pHeapEntry)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes a new heap page for the small-block heap allocator.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate page index by counting leading set bits in availability bitmap\n2. Initialize 63 free list headers as self-referencing doubly-linked lists\n3. Allocate 0x8000 bytes (32KB) via VirtualAlloc at calculated page address\n4. Initialize memory blocks with size markers (0xff0) and link pointers\n5. Link first and last blocks to the free list header at offset 0x1f8\n6. Clear usage bitmap and set availability flag for new page\n7. Increment active page counter and update heap entry flags\n\nParameters:\n- pHeapEntry (SbhHeapEntry*): Pointer to heap entry structure containing:\n  +0x04: dwFlags (bit 0 = first page active)\n  +0x08: dwAvailBitmap (page availability bitmap)\n  +0x0C: pPageBase (base address for page calculations)\n  +0x10: pHeapHeader (pointer to heap header structure)\n\nReturns:\n- Page index (0-31) on success\n- -1 on VirtualAlloc failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8000 (32768): Page size in bytes\n- 0x204 (516): Size of per-page bin structures\n- 0x144 (324): Base offset to first bin structure\n- 0x1f8 (504): Offset to free list head in bin\n- 0xff0 (4080): Block size marker for 4KB blocks\n- 0x3f (63): Number of free list headers to initialize\n- 0x1000: MEM_COMMIT flag for VirtualAlloc\n- 4: PAGE_READWRITE protection flag",
