      "name": "SetFpuControlBits",
      "signature": "uint SetFpuControlBits(void * this, void * pUnused, uint dwNewBits, uint dwMask)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Modifies specific FPU control word bits using a mask.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current FPU control word via FSTCW instruction\n2. Convert x87 control word format to logical bit layout via FUN_6ff7946a\n3. Apply masked bit operation: (current & ~mask) | (newBits & mask)\n4. Convert back to x87 format via FUN_6ff794fc\n5. Load modified control word via FLDCW instruction\n6. Return the new logical FPU control word value\n\nParameters:\n- pUnused (void*): Unused, required for __thiscall convention\n- dwNewBits (uint): New bit values to set in the control word\n- dwMask (uint): Bitmask indicating which bits to modify\n\nReturns:\n- uint: The new logical FPU control word value after modification\n\nNotes:\n- Uses helper functions to convert between x87 and logical formats\n- Classic bit manipulation pattern for selective bit updates\n- Preserves bits not specified in the mask",
