      "name": "SetFpuControlPreservingDenorm",
      "signature": "void SetFpuControlPreservingDenorm(void * this, uint dwPrecisionVal, uint dwMask)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets FPU control bits while preserving denormalized operand exception.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear bit 19 (0x80000) from dwMask to preserve denorm handling\n2. Forward to FUN_6ff7941f with modified mask\n\nParameters:\n- this (void*): FPU context pointer (via ECX, __thiscall auto-param)\n- dwPrecisionVal (uint): New precision value bits\n- dwMask (uint): Bitmask for which control bits to modify\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xfff7ffff: Mask with bit 19 cleared (~0x80000)\n- 0x80000: Denormalized operand exception mask bit (19)\n\nCalled By:\n- SetFpuDoublePrecision (with 0x10000/0x30000 for 53-bit precision)",
