      "name": "ClassifyDoubleValue",
      "signature": "int ClassifyDoubleValue(uint dwLoBits, uint dwHiBits)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Classifies an IEEE 754 double-precision floating-point value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract exponent bits (bits 52-62) from dwHiBits\n2. If exponent = 0x7FF (all 1s), call ClassifyDoubleSpecialValue for infinity/NaN\n3. If exponent = 0 and mantissa != 0, value is denormalized (subnormal)\n4. If value equals zero, return zero class with sign\n5. Otherwise return normal number class with sign\n\nParameters:\n- dwLoBits (uint): Low 32 bits of IEEE 754 double (bits 0-31)\n- dwHiBits (uint): High 32 bits of IEEE 754 double (bits 32-63)\n\nReturns:\n- 0x200: Signaling NaN (from special value = 1)\n- 0x001: Quiet NaN (from special value = 0)\n- 0x002: Infinity (from special value = 3)\n- 0x004: Negative infinity (from special value = 2)\n- 0x080/0x010: Positive/negative denormalized\n- 0x040/0x020: Positive/negative zero\n- 0x100/0x008: Positive/negative normal\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7FF0: Exponent mask for special values (max exponent)\n- 0x7FF00000: Exponent field in high word\n- 0x80000000: Sign bit mask\n- 0xFFFFF: Mantissa mask in high word",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:051b6ba20f4f945c367717acc576ceaa",
