      "name": "SetFileTranslationMode",
      "signature": "int SetFileTranslationMode(uint dwFileHandle, int nModeFlag)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Sets text/binary translation mode for a file handle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Lookup file entry from g_apFileTable using handle (index >> 5, index & 0x1f)\n2. Read current control byte at entry offset +4\n3. If nModeFlag == 0x8000 (O_TEXT): clear bit 0x80 (text mode)\n4. If nModeFlag == 0x4000 (O_BINARY): set bit 0x80 (binary mode)\n5. Otherwise: set errno = EINVAL (0x16), return -1\n6. Write modified control byte back\n7. Return previous mode based on original bit 0x80 state\n\nParameters:\n- dwFileHandle (uint): File descriptor index into g_apFileTable\n- nModeFlag (int): 0x8000 = O_TEXT, 0x4000 = O_BINARY\n\nReturns:\n- Previous mode (0x8000 for text, 0x4000 for binary)\n- -1 on error (invalid mode flag)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8000: O_TEXT flag (text translation mode)\n- 0x4000: O_BINARY flag (binary/raw mode)\n- 0x80: Binary mode bit in control byte\n- 0x24 (36): File entry stride in table\n- 0x1f: Mask for sub-index (32 entries per block)\n- 0x16: EINVAL errno value",
