      "name": "DecodeHuffmanValue",
      "signature": "int DecodeHuffmanValue(uint * pBitReader, int * pnHuffTable)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Decodes a value from a Huffman tree using a bitstream reader.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize tree index to 0\n2. Read one bit from pBitReader using gdwBitMasks lookup\n3. Increment bit position, advance byte pointer when 8 bits consumed\n4. Calculate node index: bit + current tree index\n5. If node value >= 0, return it (leaf node found)\n6. Otherwise: tree index = node index * 2 + 2 (traverse deeper)\n7. Repeat until leaf node reached\n\nParameters:\n- pBitReader (uint*): Bit reader structure [+0x0]=data ptr, [+0x8]=byte count, [+0xC]=bit pos\n- pnHuffTable (int*): Huffman decoding table; negative = branch, non-negative = leaf value\n\nReturns:\n- Decoded value from Huffman table leaf node\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8: Bits per byte, triggers byte advance\n- 0x1f: Bit position mask for shift amount",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:072df722f3c3501cb503bca82e4d66be",
