      "name": "DecomposeDoubleToComponents",
      "signature": "int * DecomposeDoubleToComponents(uint dwValueLo, uint dwValueHi, int * pnSignOut, uint * pdwDigitsOut)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Decomposes a double-precision float into sign, exponent, and digit string components.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert input double (passed as two 32-bit halves) to 80-bit extended precision via ConvertDoubleToExtended\n2. Call FUN_6ff7cf5b to format the extended float to a digit string with 17 significant digits\n3. Extract sign character and exponent from the format result structure\n4. Store sign, exponent, and digit count in the output structure (pnSignOut)\n5. Copy digit string to output buffer (pdwDigitsOut)\n6. Store pointer to digit buffer in output structure [3]\n7. Return pointer to output structure\n\nParameters:\n- dwValueLo (uint): Low 32 bits of double value\n- dwValueHi (uint): High 32 bits of double value\n- pnSignOut (int*): Output structure: [0]=sign, [1]=exponent, [2]=digit count, [3]=digits ptr\n- pdwDigitsOut (uint*): Output buffer for digit string (cast to char*)\n\nReturns:\n- int*: Pointer to pnSignOut (the filled output structure)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x11 (17): Maximum significant digits for double precision IEEE-754",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
