      "name": "HandlePowResultScaling",
      "signature": "void HandlePowResultScaling(uint dwOpcode, uint dwArgCount, uint dwArg3, uint dwArg4, uint dwArg5, uint dwArg6, uint dwArg7)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Handles FPU result scaling and error detection for pow() computation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store ST0 to stack, extract high dword (contains exponent bits)\n2. Check if exponent is zero (denormal) - scale up by 2^1536\n3. Check if exponent is 0x7ff (infinity/NaN) - scale down by 2^-1536\n4. Check FPU control word for precision mode (0x27f)\n5. Check precision exception flag (bit 5) in status word\n6. If error condition detected, dispatch to appropriate handler\n7. Two-arg functions (dwArgCount=0x1d) use __startTwoArgErrorHandling\n8. One-arg functions use __startOneArgErrorHandling\n\nParameters:\n- dwOpcode (uint): Error opcode passed to error handlers\n- dwArgCount (uint): 0x1d for two-arg functions (pow), other for one-arg\n- dwArg3-dwArg7 (uint): Additional args forwarded to error handlers\n- IMPLICIT: ST0 contains the FPU result to check/scale\n- IMPLICIT: Stack[0] contains saved FPU control word\n\nReturns:\n- void (result left in ST0 after scaling, or error handler called)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7ff00000: IEEE 754 double exponent mask (bits 20-30 of high dword)\n- 0x27f: FPU control word for extended precision, round nearest\n- 0x20: Precision exception flag in FPU status/control word\n- 0x1d: Two-argument function indicator (pow, atan2, etc.)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:0c71b5715e2e7c5f22ef70735f27ff6f",
