      "name": "strpbrk",
      "signature": "char * strpbrk(char * lpszSource, char * lpszDelimiters)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Finds the first occurrence in lpszSource of any character from lpszDelimiters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 256-bit (32-byte) character bitmap on stack to zero\n2. For each character in lpszDelimiters, set corresponding bit using BTS\n3. Scan lpszSource character by character\n4. Use BT to test if current char is in delimiter set\n5. Return pointer to first matching char, or NULL if none found\n\nParameters:\n- lpszSource (char*): String to search\n- lpszDelimiters (char*): Set of delimiter characters to find\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to first char in lpszSource that appears in lpszDelimiters\n- NULL (0) if no delimiter characters found in lpszSource\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Size of 256-bit bitmap (256/8 = 32 bytes)",
