      "name": "FindHandlerEntryById",
      "signature": "uint FindHandlerEntryById(int nHandlerId, uint dwEntryArray)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Searches an array of 12-byte handler entries for one matching the given ID.\nIterates through the handler entry array until finding an entry where offset +4\ncontains the requested handler ID, or reaches end of array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if first entry at dwEntryArray+4 matches nHandlerId\n2. If no match, loop through entries advancing by 0xC (12) bytes\n3. Stop when match found or entry address exceeds array bounds\n4. Return entry address if match confirmed, else return 0\n\nParameters:\n- nHandlerId (int): Handler type ID to search for (0x2, 0x4, 0x8, 0xb, 0xf, 0x15, 0x16)\n- dwEntryArray (uint): Base address of handler entry array\n\nReturns:\n- Address of matching entry on success\n- 0 if no entry found with matching ID\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xC (12): Handler entry stride in bytes\n- g_nHandlerEntryCount: Global containing total entry count",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
