      "name": "InitializeStdioFileTable",
      "signature": "undefined InitializeStdioFileTable(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the CRT standard I/O file handle table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate initial file table (0x480 bytes for 32 entries, 0x24 bytes each)\n2. Initialize each file entry with handle=-1, flags=0, mode=10 (text)\n3. If startup info has inherited handles (cbReserved2/lpReserved2):\n   a. Expand file table if needed (up to 0x800 max handles)\n   b. Copy valid inherited handles with flags to file table\n4. Initialize stdin/stdout/stderr (indices 0-2):\n   a. Get standard handles via GetStdHandle\n   b. Set flags: 0x81=open, 0x40=device, 0x08=pipe, 0x80=inherited\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies global g_apFileTable and g_nMaxFileHandles)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x480: File table size (32 entries * 0x24 bytes)\n- 0x24 (36): Size of each file entry structure\n- 0x20: Initial max file handles (32)\n- 0x800: Maximum handle count limit (2048)\n- 0xfffffff6 (-10): STD_INPUT_HANDLE\n- 0xfffffff5 (-11): STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE\n- 0xfffffff4 (-12): STD_ERROR_HANDLE\n- 0x81: FOPEN flag (file is open)\n- 0x40: FDEV flag (file is device)\n- 0x08: FPIPE flag (file is pipe)\n- 0x80: FINHRT flag (inherited handle)\n\nRelated Functions: CRTDllMain, SetHandleCount, GetStartupInfoA",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
