      "name": "ConvertFlagsToFpuControlWord",
      "signature": "uint ConvertFlagsToFpuControlWord(uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Converts abstract FPU flags back to x87 FPU control word format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Maps exception mask bits (Invalid,Denormal,ZeroDiv,Overflow,Underflow,Precision)\n2. Converts precision control (0x100=24-bit,0x200=53-bit,0x300=64-bit)\n3. Converts rounding control (0=truncate,0x10000=round-down,default=nearest)\n4. Maps infinity control flag\n\nParameters:\n- dwFlags (uint): Abstract FPU control flags\n\nReturns:\n- x87 FPU control word value\n\nFlag Bits (Input -> Output):\n- 0x10 -> 0x01: Invalid exception mask\n- 0x08 -> 0x04: Denormal exception mask\n- 0x04 -> 0x08: Zero divide exception mask\n- 0x02 -> 0x10: Overflow exception mask\n- 0x01 -> 0x20: Underflow exception mask\n- 0x80000 -> 0x02: Precision exception mask\n- 0x100 -> 0x400: 24-bit precision\n- 0x200 -> 0x800: 53-bit precision\n- 0x300 -> 0xC00: 64-bit precision\n- 0x00 (rounding) -> 0x300: Truncate\n- 0x10000 -> 0x200: Round down\n- 0x40000 -> 0x1000: Infinity control",
