      "name": "InitCrtHeap",
      "signature": "int InitCrtHeap(int nSerializeAccess)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes the CRT heap for runtime memory allocation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create process heap with HeapCreate (serialized if fSerializeAccess==0)\n2. Store heap handle in g_hProcessHeap global\n3. Determine heap mode via FUN_6ff74fb4\n4. Mode 3: Allocate 0x3F8 bytes via FUN_6ff75201\n5. Mode 2: Initialize via FUN_6ff75d48\n6. On init failure, destroy heap and return 0\n\nParameters:\n- fSerializeAccess: If 0, creates serialized heap (thread-safe); else unserialized\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success, 0 on failure (heap creation or initialization failed)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1000: Initial heap size (4KB)\n- 0x3F8: Allocation size for mode 3 (1016 bytes)\n- Mode 2/3: Heap initialization modes from FUN_6ff74fb4",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
