      "name": "FlushAndResetStreamBuffer",
      "signature": "void FlushAndResetStreamBuffer(int nBufferReady, int * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Conditionally flushes and resets stream buffer after formatted output.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if buffer init succeeded (nBufferReady != 0)\n2. Verify stream flags indicate flush needed (flag 0x10 at offset 0xd)\n3. Call FlushWriteBuffer to write pending data\n4. Clear stream state flags (AND 0xee at offset 0xd)\n5. Reset buffer pointers: offset 0x18, 0x0, 0x8 all cleared to 0\n\nParameters:\n- nBufferReady (int): Non-zero if InitStdStreamBuffer succeeded\n- pStream (int*): FILE structure pointer\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10: Buffer flush needed flag (tested at pStream+0xd)\n- 0xee: Flag clear mask (clears bits 0x01 and 0x10)\n- 0x18, 0x08, 0x00: Buffer count/position fields in FILE struct",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:1824f16f2819b687d45722a6208240bd",
