      "name": "HandlePowerSpecialCases",
      "signature": "int HandlePowerSpecialCases(int nBaseLo, int nBaseHi, double dExponent, double * pdResult)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Handles IEEE 754 special cases for power(base, exponent) computation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reconstruct base double from nBaseLo/nBaseHi, take absolute value\n2. Check if exponent is +Inf or -Inf, handle special cases\n3. For -Inf base with integer exponent: call FUN_6ff7434c for parity\n4. Return appropriate result (0, 1, +Inf, -Inf, NaN)\n\nParameters:\n- nBaseLo (int): Low 32 bits of base double\n- nBaseHi (int): High 32 bits of base double  \n- dExponent (double): Power exponent\n- pdResult (double*): Output result pointer\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if handled as exact result (NaN output)\n- 0 if handled with computed result\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7ff00000: IEEE 754 +Infinity high bits\n- 0xfff00000 (-0x100000): IEEE 754 -Infinity high bits",
