      "name": "MeasureCpuClockMHz",
      "signature": "ulonglong MeasureCpuClockMHz(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "ulonglong",
      "comment": "Measures CPU clock frequency in MHz using RDTSC instruction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current thread priority\n2. Record initial tick count and performance counter\n3. Read initial TSC via RDTSC\n4. Busy-wait until at least 10ms elapsed\n5. Read final TSC and performance counter\n6. Calculate MHz: (TSC_delta * PerfFreq) / (PerfCounter_delta * 1000000)\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- CPU clock frequency in MHz as ulonglong\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7fffffff: THREAD_PRIORITY_ERROR_RETURN\n- 0xa (10): Minimum wait time in milliseconds\n- 0xf4240 (1000000): Microseconds per second divisor",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
