      "name": "FormatDecimalString",
      "signature": "char * FormatDecimalString(char * szBuffer, size_t nDecimalPlaces, int * pNumInfo, char cPadFlag)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Formats numeric string with decimal point and sign.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If cPadFlag set and digit count-1 equals decimal places, add trailing '0'\n2. If number is negative (sign == 0x2d), prepend '-' to buffer\n3. If digit count <= 0, insert leading '0' before decimal\n4. If decimal places > 0, insert decimal point character\n5. If digit count < 0, pad with leading zeros after decimal point\n\nParameters:\n- szBuffer (char*): Output buffer containing digit string\n- nDecimalPlaces (size_t): Number of digits after decimal point\n- pNumInfo (int*): Number info struct [0]=sign (0x2d='-'), [4]=digit count\n- cPadFlag (char): Non-zero enables trailing zero padding\n\nReturns:\n- szBuffer pointer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2d (45): ASCII '-' minus sign\n- 0x30 (48): ASCII '0' for zero padding",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
