      "name": "HandleFpuExceptionFlags",
      "signature": "bool HandleFpuExceptionFlags(uint dwExceptFlags, double * pdValue, uint dwRounding)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Handles FPU exception flags and converts special values based on rounding mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract exception flags (bits 0-4) from dwExceptFlags\n2. Check for overflow (bit 3) with rounding enabled - clear overflow flag\n3. Check for underflow (bit 2) with rounding enabled - clear underflow flag\n4. Check for invalid (bit 0) with divide-by-zero enabled - set infinity with sign\n5. Check for denormalize (bit 1) with inexact enabled - denormalize mantissa\n6. Check for inexact (bit 4) with stack fault enabled - clear inexact flag\n7. Return true if all exception flags handled (cleared)\n\nParameters:\n- dwExceptFlags (uint): FPU exception status bits (0x1=invalid, 0x2=denorm, 0x4=zerodiv, 0x8=overflow, 0x10=inexact)\n- pdValue (double*): Pointer to floating-point value to modify\n- dwRounding (uint): Rounding control mode (bits 10-11: 0x400=up, 0x800=down, 0xc00=truncate)\n\nReturns:\n- true if all flagged exceptions were handled\n- false if any exception flag remains set\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1f: Mask for 5 exception flags\n- 0xc00: Rounding mode bits mask\n- 0x400: Round up mode\n- 0x800: Round down mode\n- 0x600 (1536): Exponent bias adjustment for denormalization\n- 0x432 (1074): Minimum exponent threshold\n- 0x3fd (1021): Denormalization shift limit",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:21ebbf809f077a14550cdc7271d10c0f",
