      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Destroys a DataArray and releases it back to the memory pool.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Zeros entire DataArray structure (0x48 DWORDs = 288 bytes)\n2. Calls ReleasePoolAllocation to free memory back to pool 0x4B\n\nParameters:\n- pDataArray (uint*): Pointer to DataArray structure to destroy\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nNotes:\n- Uses REP STOSD for efficient memory zeroing\n- Pool ID 0x4B (75) corresponds to DataArray allocations\n- Source: DataArrays.cpp",
