      "name": "HeapAllocDispatch",
      "signature": "void * HeapAllocDispatch(size_t cbSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Internal heap allocation dispatcher for CRT malloc.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check heap mode in DAT_6ffa2ca4 (3=small block, 2=page alloc)\n2. Mode 3: If size <= threshold, allocate from small block heap via FUN_6ff7559d\n3. Mode 2: Round size to 16-byte boundary, allocate via page allocator FUN_6ff76040\n4. Fallback: Use HeapAlloc from DAT_6ffa2ca0 process heap\n\nParameters:\n- cbSize (size_t): Number of bytes to allocate\n\nReturns:\n- void*: Pointer to allocated memory, NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10 (16): Minimum allocation and alignment boundary\n- 0xF/0xFFFFFFF0: Masks for 16-byte alignment\n- 9: Critical section index for heap lock",
