      "name": "InitializeWorkerThread",
      "signature": "void InitializeWorkerThread(int * pContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes and starts a worker thread for the given context structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validates pContext is non-NULL and not already initialized (*pContext == 0)\n2. Clears shutdown flag at pContext[0x48] (offset 0x120)\n3. Creates an unnamed auto-reset event, stores handle at pContext[0x45] (offset 0x114)\n4. Creates worker thread running FUN_6ff616f0, stores handle at *pContext\n5. Thread ID is stored at pContext[1] (offset 0x4)\n6. Waits in a polling loop (10ms Sleep) until thread signals ready (WaitForSingleObject returns 0)\n\nParameters:\n- pContext (int*): Thread context structure containing thread handles and state\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nStructure Layout (pContext offsets):\n- 0x000: Thread handle (HANDLE)\n- 0x004: Thread ID (DWORD)\n- 0x114: Event handle (HANDLE)\n- 0x120: Shutdown flag (DWORD)",
