      "name": "IsUnitModeActiveOrMoving",
      "signature": "int IsUnitModeActiveOrMoving(void * pUnit)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Checks if unit mode indicates active or moving state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return 0 if pUnit is NULL\n2. Read mode value at offset 0x86c\n3. Return 1 if mode is 1 (active) or 2 (moving)\n4. Return 0 otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (void*): Pointer to unit structure\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if unit mode is active (1) or moving (2)\n- 0 if pUnit is NULL or mode is invalid\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x86c: Unit mode field offset\n- 1: Active mode\n- 2: Moving mode",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
