      "name": "UngetStreamChar",
      "signature": "uint UngetStreamChar(uint dwChar, int * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Push a character back onto an input stream.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return EOF (-1) if dwChar is EOF\n2. Check stream flags: must be in read mode (0x1) or unbuffered (0x80) without write mode (0x2)\n3. Allocate buffer if none exists (pStream[2] == 0)\n4. If buffer position equals buffer base and count > 0, return EOF (can't unget)\n5. If 0x40 flag set (unget mode): verify char matches else fail\n6. Decrement position pointer, store character\n7. Increment count, update flags (clear 0x10, set 0x1)\n8. Return low byte of character\n\nParameters:\n- dwChar (uint): Character to push back (0-255), or EOF (0xFFFFFFFF)\n- pStream (int*): Stream structure pointer\n\nReturns:\n- Low byte of dwChar (0-255) on success\n- 0xFFFFFFFF (EOF) on failure\n\nStructure Layout (pStream):\n- [0] pCurPos: Current buffer position pointer\n- [1] nCount: Character count in buffer\n- [2] pBase: Buffer base address\n- [3] dwFlags: Stream state flags\n\nFlag Bits:\n- 0x01: Read mode active\n- 0x02: Write mode active\n- 0x10: (Cleared on unget)\n- 0x40: Unget verification mode\n- 0x80: Unbuffered I/O mode",
