      "name": "DivideExtendedPrecision",
      "signature": "uint DivideExtendedPrecision(uint dwDividendLo, uint dwDividendHi, ushort wDividendExp, uint dwDivisorLo, uint dwDivisorHi, uint dwDivisorExp)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Extended precision floating-point division helper.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load dividend and divisor as 80-bit extended doubles from stack\n2. Check for special cases: zero dividend, zero/denormal exponents\n3. For normalized numbers, perform direct FDIVP\n4. For denormal operands, normalize by multiplying with scale constants\n5. Handle infinity (0x7FFF exponent) and NaN cases via lookup table\n\nParameters:\n- dwDividendLo (uint): Low 32 bits of dividend mantissa\n- dwDividendHi (uint): High 32 bits of dividend mantissa\n- wDividendExp (ushort): Dividend exponent (15 bits, bit 15 = sign)\n- dwDivisorLo (uint): Low 32 bits of divisor mantissa\n- dwDivisorHi (uint): High 32 bits of divisor mantissa\n- dwDivisorExp (uint): Divisor exponent and sign\n\nReturns:\n- Exponent/status of result (0 for zero, 0x7FFF for infinity/NaN)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7FFF: Infinity/NaN exponent mask\n- 0xE000000: Overflow detection mask after shift\n- 0x33F, 0xF3FF: FPU control word masks for precision control\n- DAT_6ff86850: Lookup table for special case handling\n- DAT_6ff86860: Normalization scale factor\n- DAT_6ff86868: Denormal normalization multiplier",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
