      "name": "CallocHeapAlloc",
      "signature": "void * CallocHeapAlloc(uint dwCount, uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates zero-initialized memory for an array (calloc-style).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute total size as dwCount * dwSize\n2. Align size to 16-byte boundary (add 0xF, AND with 0xFFFFFFF0)\n3. Check heap mode (g_dwHeapMode):\n   - Mode 3: Use SbhAllocBlock for small allocations (<= g_cbSmallBlockThreshold)\n   - Mode 2: Use SbhAllocFromNodes for page-aligned allocations (<= g_cbPageAllocThreshold)\n4. Fall back to HeapAlloc with HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY flag (0x8)\n5. If allocation fails and g_pfnNewHandler set, invoke callback and retry\n\nParameters:\n- dwCount (uint): Number of elements to allocate\n- dwSize (uint): Size of each element in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to zero-initialized memory on success, NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xFFFFFFE1: Maximum valid allocation size (~4GB - 31 bytes)\n- 0x8: HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY flag for HeapAlloc\n- 0x9: Critical section index for heap lock",
