      "name": "WriteCharToBuffer",
      "signature": "void WriteCharToBuffer(uint dwChar, int * pStream, int * pnCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Writes a single character to a buffered stream structure.\nUsed by printf-style formatting functions to output characters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Decrement buffer space counter at pStream[1]\n2. If counter goes negative, buffer is full - call PutCharToStream to flush\n3. Otherwise write low byte of dwChar to current buffer position\n4. Advance buffer pointer at pStream[0]\n5. Return masked char value (dwChar & 0xFF) on success\n6. On error (return == -1), set *pnCount to -1 to flag failure\n7. On success, increment *pnCount to track total chars written\n\nParameters:\n- dwChar (uint): Character to write (only low byte is used)\n- pStream (int*): Stream buffer structure [buffer_ptr, space_remaining, ...]\n- pnCount (int*): Pointer to running output character count\n\nReturns:\n- void (error status communicated via *pnCount = -1)",
