      "name": "InitializeTimezoneData",
      "signature": "undefined InitializeTimezoneData(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes timezone data from TZ environment variable or Windows API.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Lock critical section 0xC\n2. Reset timezone cache flags to -1 (invalid)\n3. Check TZ environment variable via FUN_6ff7d37c(\"TZ\")\n4. If TZ not set:\n   a. Call GetTimeZoneInformation Windows API\n   b. Calculate g_nTimezoneOffset = Bias * 60 seconds\n   c. Add StandardBias if applicable\n   d. Set g_fDstEnabled and _g_nDstOffset from DST info\n   e. Convert wide timezone names to multibyte via WideCharToMultiByte\n5. If TZ set:\n   a. Cache TZ string in DAT_6ffa18c4\n   b. Parse format: \"STD[+|-]offset[:minutes[:seconds]][DST]\"\n   c. Extract standard timezone name (3 chars)\n   d. Parse hours (multiply by 0xE10 = 3600 seconds)\n   e. Parse optional minutes (multiply by 0x3C = 60)\n   f. Parse optional seconds\n   g. Negate if minus sign prefix\n   h. Extract DST name if present\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xC: Critical section index for timezone data\n- 0x3C (60): Seconds per minute\n- 0xE10 (3600): Seconds per hour\n- 0x220: WC_NO_BEST_FIT_CHARS | WC_COMPOSITECHECK\n- 0x3F (63): Max timezone name length\n- 0x2D (45): ASCII '-' minus sign\n- 0x3A (58): ASCII ':' colon separator",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
