      "name": "FlushWriteBuffer",
      "signature": "int FlushWriteBuffer(int * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Flushes buffered write data to the underlying file descriptor.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check stream is in write mode ((flags & 3) == 2) with dirty buffer (flags & 0x108)\n2. Calculate bytes to write: current_pos - buffer_base\n3. Write bytes via FUN_6ff78085(file_handle, buffer_base, count)\n4. On success: clear write mode flag (0x02) if no-buffer mode (0x80)\n5. On failure: set error flag (0x20), return -1\n6. Reset: clear count field, reset current_pos to buffer_base\n\nParameters:\n- pStream (int*): FILE structure pointer\n  - [0]: current buffer position\n  - [1]: remaining count (cleared to 0)\n  - [2]: buffer base pointer\n  - [3]: stream flags\n  - [4]: file descriptor/handle\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success or no flush needed\n- -1 on write failure (error flag 0x20 set)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x02: Write mode flag\n- 0x20: Error flag (set on write failure)\n- 0x80: No-buffer mode flag\n- 0x108: Dirty buffer indicator mask",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
