      "name": "SbhAllocFromBlock",
      "signature": "void * SbhAllocFromBlock(int * pBlockDesc, uint dwAvailable, uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates memory from a Small Block Heap (SBH) block descriptor.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If remaining space at current position >= dwSize, allocate there\n2. Otherwise, scan block for free runs (sequences of zero bytes)\n3. Find first free run >= dwSize, coalesce if needed\n4. Mark allocation with size byte, update descriptor\n5. Return pointer offset from descriptor base\n\nParameters:\n- pBlockDesc (int*): Block descriptor [0]=next free ptr, [1]=remaining bytes\n- dwAvailable (uint): Available space in current region\n- dwSize (uint): Requested allocation size (1-240 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n- Encoded pointer on success (ptr*16 - desc*15)\n- 0 on failure (no space found)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xF8 (248): Block end offset from descriptor\n- 0x8: Header size / allocation granularity",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:4f3543287939943021eaf1632a1582f1",
