      "name": "ParseCommandLineToArgv",
      "signature": "void ParseCommandLineToArgv(byte * pbCmdLine, char * * ppszArgv, byte * pbBuffer, int * pnArgCount, int * pnCharCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Parses a command line string into argv-style array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize arg count to 1 (for program name), char count to 0\n2. Store buffer pointer as argv[0] if ppszArgv provided\n3. Parse first argument (program name) handling quoted strings\n4. Loop through remaining arguments separated by whitespace\n5. Handle backslash-quote escaping per Windows conventions\n6. Null-terminate each argument and increment counters\n7. Null-terminate argv array and increment arg count\n\nParameters:\n- pbCmdLine (byte*): Input command line string to parse\n- ppszArgv (char**): Output argv array (NULL for counting pass)\n- pbBuffer (byte*): Output buffer for argument strings (NULL for counting)\n- pnArgCount (int*): Output argument count (argc)\n- pnCharCount (int*): Output total character count including nulls\n\nReturns:\n- void (outputs via pointer parameters)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x22 (34): Double quote character\n- 0x5c (92): Backslash character\n- 0x20 (32): Space character\n- 0x9: Tab character\n- 0x4: MBCS lead byte flag in character type table\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Called twice: first with NULL buffers to count, then to populate\n- Handles Windows-style backslash escaping before quotes\n- Uses g_abCharTypeTable for MBCS lead byte detection",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
