      "name": "AreBitsZeroFromPos",
      "signature": "bool AreBitsZeroFromPos(uint * pdwBitmap, int nBitPos)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Checks if all bits from a given position to the end of a 96-bit bitmap are zero.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create mask for bits from nBitPos to end of current DWORD\n2. Check if any masked bits are set in current DWORD, return false if so\n3. Loop through remaining DWORDs (up to index 2), return false if any non-zero\n\nParameters:\n- pdwBitmap (uint*): Pointer to 3-DWORD (96-bit) bitmap array\n- nBitPos (int): Starting bit position (0-95) to check from\n\nReturns:\n- true if all bits from nBitPos to bit 95 are zero\n- false if any bit in that range is set\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Bits per DWORD\n- 0x1f (31): Mask for bit position within DWORD\n- 3: Number of DWORDs in bitmap (96 bits total)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:546b5c43c0effce0a0403e1069ea2e2c",
