      "name": "ToUpperInPlace",
      "signature": "void ToUpperInPlace(char * szBuffer, int nMaxLen)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts string characters to uppercase in-place using lookup table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through string until null terminator or nMaxLen reached\n2. Replace each character with its uppercase equivalent from g_abUpperCaseTable\n3. Stop at end of string or buffer limit\n\nParameters:\n- szBuffer (char*): Null-terminated string to convert in-place\n- nMaxLen (int): Maximum number of characters to process\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10216: Adds key to string hash index, calls this for case normalization\n- Ordinal_10217: Looks up key in string hash index, calls this for case normalization",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
