      "name": "ToUpperCaseLocaleAware",
      "signature": "uint ToUpperCaseLocaleAware(void * this, uint dwChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Converts a character to uppercase using locale-aware mapping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If no locale configured, use simple ASCII conversion (a-z to A-Z)\n2. Check if character is in single-byte range (< 0x100)\n3. For single-byte: check character type table for lowercase flag (bit 1)\n4. Build MBCS byte sequence: single byte or lead+trail byte pair\n5. Call LCMapString wrapper with LCMAP_UPPERCASE (0x200) flag\n6. Extract result from output buffer (1 or 2 bytes based on length)\n\nParameters:\n- this (void*): CRT locale context pointer passed to callees\n- dwChar (uint): Character code to convert to uppercase\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Uppercase character code, or original if not lowercase\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x60/0x7b: ASCII lowercase bounds ('a'-1 / 'z'+1)\n- 0x20: ASCII case offset (subtract to convert lowercase to uppercase)\n- 0x100: Single-byte character boundary\n- 0x200: LCMAP_UPPERCASE flag for LCMapString\n- 0x80: Lead byte indicator bit in character type table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
