      "name": "AllocateFileDescriptor",
      "signature": "uint AllocateFileDescriptor(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Allocates and returns a free file descriptor from the CRT file table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Lock file table critical section (index 0x12)\n2. Scan existing tables for a free entry (flags byte bit 0 == 0)\n3. If found, initialize critical section if needed, mark entry\n4. If all tables full, allocate new 0x480-byte table (32 entries)\n5. Initialize new table entries and call helper FUN_6ff7bcea\n6. Unlock critical section and return descriptor\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- File descriptor index on success (0 to g_dwMaxFileDesc-1)\n- 0xFFFFFFFF if allocation fails\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x12: File table critical section index\n- 0x11: Entry init critical section index\n- 0x24 (36): File entry stride (sizeof entry)\n- 0x480 (1152): Table size (32 entries * 36 bytes)\n- 0x20 (32): Entries per table\n- 0x120 (288): Entries per table in DWORDs (32*9)\n\nStructure Layout (entry at offset 0x24*n):\n+0x00: DWORD  - OS file handle (0xFFFFFFFF = invalid)\n+0x04: BYTE   - flags (bit 0 = in use)\n+0x05: BYTE   - text mode (10 = LF mode)\n+0x08: DWORD  - critical section init flag\n+0x0C: CRITICAL_SECTION (24 bytes)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:5a19e694488816d4876bc457287c101c",
