      "name": "LockCriticalSectionByIndex",
      "signature": "void LockCriticalSectionByIndex(int nLockIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Acquires a critical section lock by index, lazily initializing it if needed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if critical section at index exists in g_apCritSectArray\n2. If not, allocate 0x18 bytes (sizeof CRITICAL_SECTION)\n3. Recursively lock index 0x11 to protect initialization\n4. Double-check slot is still empty (race condition guard)\n5. Initialize the critical section and store pointer\n6. Unlock index 0x11\n7. Enter the critical section\n\nParameters:\n- nLockIndex (int): Index into global critical section array\n\nReturns:\n- void (acquires lock, no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x18 (24): sizeof(CRITICAL_SECTION)\n- 0x11 (17): Master lock index for protecting array initialization",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:5ba7875cbad7a3d5fce31ff25fd40455",
