      "name": "SetBitInArray",
      "signature": "void SetBitInArray(byte * pbBitArray, uint dwBitIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets a bit in a bit array at the specified index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate byte offset (dwBitIndex >> 3)\n2. Calculate bit position within byte (dwBitIndex & 7)\n3. OR the target byte with the bitmask from gdwBitMasks\n\nParameters:\n- pbBitArray (byte*): Pointer to the bit array\n- dwBitIndex (uint): Zero-based bit index to set\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nRelated Functions:\n- TestBitInArray (Ordinal 10119): Tests if a bit is set",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:5e8ac3c5b51c563cb223a17efc5e174a",
