      "name": "SetEnvironmentEntry",
      "signature": "int SetEnvironmentEntry(char * szEntry, int nSyncToSystem)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Sets or removes an environment variable in the internal environment array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Parse entry to find '=' separator; validate format (NAME=VALUE)\n2. Initialize environment array if NULL (allocate or convert from wide)\n3. Search for existing entry by name prefix\n4. If value empty (NAME=): remove existing entry, compact array\n5. If value present: add/replace entry in array, reallocate as needed\n6. If fSyncToSystem: call SetEnvironmentVariableA to sync Windows env\n\nParameters:\n- szEntry (char*): Environment string in \"NAME=VALUE\" or \"NAME=\" format\n- fSyncToSystem (int): If non-zero, also update Windows environment\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success\n- -1 on error (NULL input, malloc failure, invalid format)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6ff7dcf7: Search for entry by name prefix\n- FUN_6ff7ddb6: Find '=' character (strchr variant)\n- ConvertWideEnvironToMultiByte: Wide-to-multibyte conversion",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
