      "name": "SprintfToBuffer",
      "signature": "int SprintfToBuffer(char * szBuffer, byte * pbFormat, ...)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Formats a string into buffer using printf-style format specifier.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize buffer context with start pointer and MAX_INT capacity\n2. Call internal format processor (FUN_6ff74762) with varargs\n3. If capacity overflow, flush/finalize via FUN_6ff7464a\n4. Otherwise null-terminate at current position\n5. Return bytes written\n\nParameters:\n- pszBuffer (char*): Output buffer for formatted string\n- pbFormat (byte*): Printf-style format string\n- ... : Variadic format arguments\n\nReturns:\n- int: Number of characters written (excluding null)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x42: Buffer type indicator 'B'\n- 0x7FFFFFFF: MAX_INT initial capacity (effectively unlimited)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
