      "name": "GetSlotEntryCount",
      "signature": "int GetSlotEntryCount(void * pContext, int nSlotIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Counts entries in a slot's linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nSlotIndex against slot count at offset 0x87c\n2. Return -1 if index out of bounds\n3. Acquire critical section at offset 0x854 via Ordinal_10050\n4. Get list head from slot array at offset 0x870[nSlotIndex]\n5. Traverse linked list following next pointer at offset 0x5bc\n6. Release critical section and return count\n\nParameters:\n- pContext (void*): Context structure with slot array and critical section\n- nSlotIndex (int): Index into slot array\n\nReturns:\n- Entry count >= 0 on success\n- -1 if nSlotIndex >= slot count\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x854: Critical section offset in context\n- 0x870: Slot array pointer offset in context\n- 0x87c: Slot count offset in context\n- 0x5bc: Next pointer offset in list entry",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
