      "name": "InvokeTlsCallbackAndExit",
      "signature": "undefined InvokeTlsCallbackAndExit(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Invokes TLS callback and terminates with runtime error.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Sets up SEH frame for exception handling\n2. Gets TLS data via GetOrAllocTlsData()\n3. If TLS callback at offset 0x60 exists, invokes it\n4. Calls FUN_6ff7b9f2 which shows runtime error 10 and exits\n\nParameters:\n- None\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x60: TLS callback function pointer offset (0x18 * 4)\n- -1/0xFFFFFFFF: SEH cleanup state marker\n\nReturns:\n- Does not return; terminates via __exit(3)",
