      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword *",
      "comment": "Gets or allocates thread-local storage (TLS) data for the current thread.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current error code via GetLastError\n2. Try TlsGetValue to retrieve existing TLS data\n3. If NULL, allocate 0x74 (116) bytes via FUN_6ff7b8b5\n4. Store allocation in TLS slot via TlsSetValue\n5. Initialize fields via InitTlsDefaultFields\n6. Set thread ID at offset 0x0 and -1 at offset 0x4\n7. On allocation failure, call __amsg_exit(0x10)\n8. Restore error code via SetLastError\n\nParameters:\n- None\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to TLS data structure (116 bytes)\n- Never returns NULL (calls __amsg_exit on failure)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x74 (116): TLS data structure size\n- 0x10: Runtime error code for TLS allocation failure\n- 0xFFFFFFFF: Initial value at offset 0x4 (likely exception state)",
