      "name": "AllocateStreamBuffer",
      "signature": "void AllocateStreamBuffer(uint * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Allocates a 4KB buffer for stream I/O operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment global open stream count\n2. Attempt to malloc 0x1000 (4096) bytes\n3. If allocation succeeds: set flag 0x8 (allocated), size 0x1000\n4. If allocation fails: use internal 2-byte buffer at pStream+5, set flag 0x4\n5. Initialize buffer pointer and clear bytes-available counter\n\nParameters:\n- pStream (uint*): Stream structure pointer with layout:\n  [0x00] pCurrent - Current buffer position\n  [0x04] nAvailable - Bytes available in buffer\n  [0x08] pBuffer - Buffer pointer\n  [0x0C] dwFlags - Stream flags (0x4=internal, 0x8=allocated)\n  [0x14] abInternal[2] - Internal fallback buffer\n  [0x18] nBufSize - Buffer size\n\nReturns:\n- void (buffer info stored in pStream structure)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1000: Default buffer size (4KB)\n- 0x4: Flag for internal buffer mode\n- 0x8: Flag for allocated buffer mode\n- 0x2: Internal buffer size (2 bytes)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
