      "name": "strcpy",
      "signature": "char * strcpy(char * szDest, char * szSrc)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Copies source string to destination buffer. Optimized DWORD-at-a-time copy.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Align source pointer to 4-byte boundary, copying bytes until aligned\n2. Read 4 bytes at a time and check for null terminator using bit manipulation\n3. When null found, determine which byte position and copy remaining bytes\n4. Return pointer to destination buffer\n\nParameters:\n- szDest (char*): Destination buffer (must be large enough)\n- szSrc (char*): Null-terminated source string\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to szDest (for chaining)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7efefeff: Null byte detection mask complement\n- 0x81010100: Null byte detection result mask",
