      "name": "ParseBondHeader",
      "signature": "int * ParseBondHeader(int * * ppBuffer, uint * pdwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Parses a BOND header from buffer and advances buffer pointer past it.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check minimum size (8 bytes for header)\n2. Validate BOND signature (0x444E4F42)\n3. Calculate total size: count * 12 + 8\n4. Verify size <= 0x400 and fits in buffer\n5. Advance buffer pointer, decrement size\n\nParameters:\n- ppBuffer (int**): Pointer to buffer pointer, advanced on success\n- pdwSize (uint*): Pointer to remaining size, decremented on success\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to BOND header on success\n- NULL on failure (bad signature, size violation)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x444E4F42: \"BOND\" signature (little-endian)\n- 0xC (12): Size per entry in BOND table\n- 0x8: BOND header size (signature + count)\n- 0x400 (1024): Maximum allowed BOND size",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:716e37473eb5a60b950d65ba0bcefe75",
