      "name": "BitwiseAndBuffers",
      "signature": "void BitwiseAndBuffers(int nSrc1, int nSrc2, int nDest, int nBitCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Performs bitwise AND on two byte buffers and stores result in destination.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert bit count to byte count: nBytes = (nBitCount + 7) / 8\n2. Calculate DWORD-aligned chunks: nChunks = (nBytes + 3) / 4 * 4\n3. Process DWORD chunks in loop: pDest[i] = pSrc1[i] & pSrc2[i]\n4. Handle remainder bytes (1-3) based on (nBytes mod 4)\n5. Fall-through switch handles 3->2->1 byte remainders\n\nParameters:\n- nSrc1 (int): Pointer to first source byte buffer\n- nSrc2 (int): Pointer to second source byte buffer\n- nDest (int): Pointer to destination buffer for AND result\n- nBitCount (int): Number of bits to process (rounds up to bytes)\n\nReturns:\n- void (result written to nDest buffer)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7: Bitmask for rounding up to byte boundary\n- 0x3: Bitmask for rounding up to DWORD boundary",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
