      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the CRT command line argument array (__argv).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls subsystem initialization if not already done\n2. Gets module filename via GetModuleFileNameA\n3. Uses command line or module path as argv[0] source\n4. Calls FUN_6ff78fad to count args and calculate buffer size\n5. Allocates memory for argv array + string storage\n6. Calls FUN_6ff78fad again to populate arrays\n7. Stores argv pointer and argc-1 in globals\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- void (sets g_pArgv=argv, g_nArgc=argc-1)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x104 (260): MAX_PATH buffer size\n- 0x8: __amsg_exit error code for memory allocation failure",
