      "name": "ResizeHeapBlock",
      "signature": "int ResizeHeapBlock(int nHeapState, int * pFreeEntry, byte * pbBlock, uint dwNewSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Resizes a heap block in place by adjusting size marker and free space tracking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate page info pointer from block address using 4KB page indexing\n2. If shrinking: Update block size byte, add freed space to page info\n3. If growing: Verify extension fits in page (0xf8 limit), verify extension bytes are zero\n4. Update free entry pointer if it falls within the resized region\n5. Recalculate consecutive free bytes after new block end\n\nParameters:\n- nHeapState (int): Heap state structure with page base at offset 0x10\n- pFreeEntry (int*): Free space tracking entry [ptr, free_count]\n- pbBlock (byte*): Block to resize (first byte is size)\n- dwNewSize (uint): New size for the block\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success, 0 on failure (size unchanged or growth impossible)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10: Offset to page base in heap state\n- 0x18: Offset to page info array in heap state\n- 0xc (12): Page index shift (4KB pages)\n- 0xf1 (241): Marker for modified page info\n- 0xf8 (248): Maximum block extent within page",
