      "name": "StartWorkerThread",
      "signature": "HANDLE StartWorkerThread(void * pCtx)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "HANDLE",
      "comment": "Starts a worker thread for the given context structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pCtx is non-NULL and not already running (offset 0x0 == 0)\n2. Initialize status field at offset 0x120 to 0\n3. Create unnamed auto-reset event, store handle at offset 0x114\n4. Create thread with SpawnStormWorkerThread, store handle at offset 0x0\n5. Store thread ID at offset 0x4\n\nParameters:\n- pCtx (void*): Context structure with thread state fields\n\nReturns:\n- Thread handle on success, NULL if pCtx is NULL or already running\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x114: Event handle offset in context\n- 0x120: Status/flag field offset in context",
