      "name": "CompareStringsIgnoreCase",
      "signature": "int CompareStringsIgnoreCase(void * this, void * pUnused, byte * pszStr1, byte * pszStr2)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Compares two byte strings case-insensitively.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If no locale set (g_dwLocaleId == 0): Fast ASCII-only path\n   - Loops through both strings byte-by-byte\n   - Converts A-Z (0x41-0x5A) to lowercase by adding 0x20\n   - Returns comparison result when mismatch found\n2. With locale active: Locale-aware path\n   - Acquires locale lock via FUN_6ff7372d(0x13)\n   - For each byte pair, calls ToLowerCaseLocaleAware()\n   - Releases lock via FUN_6ff7378e(0x13) or ref count\n\nParameters:\n- pUnused (void*): Unused __thiscall context\n- pszStr1 (byte*): First string to compare\n- pszStr2 (byte*): Second string to compare\n\nReturns:\n- -1 if pszStr1 < pszStr2\n- 0 if strings are equal\n- 1 if pszStr1 > pszStr2\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x13 (19): Critical section index for locale lock\n- 0x41-0x5A: ASCII 'A'-'Z' range\n- 0x20: ASCII case offset",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
