      "name": "CRTDllMain",
      "signature": "int CRTDllMain(void * pDllHandle, int nReason)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "CRT DLL entry point handler for process/thread attach/detach.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check nReason for attach/detach notification type\n2. DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH (1): Call GetVersion(), init heap via FUN_6ff750fc,\n   parse version into major/minor/build, init subsystems, get command line,\n   call static initializers, increment g_nCRTInitCount\n3. DLL_PROCESS_DETACH (0): If g_nCRTInitCount > 0, decrement it, run\n   ExitWithCleanup if not already exiting, cleanup thread and heap\n4. DLL_THREAD_DETACH (3): Call FUN_6ff7729f for thread-local cleanup\n5. Return 1 on success, 0 on initialization failure\n\nParameters:\n- pDllHandle (void*): DLL module handle, unused by this function\n- nReason (int): Reason code (0=detach, 1=attach, 3=thread_detach)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Success or unrecognized reason code\n- 0: Heap or subsystem initialization failed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0: DLL_PROCESS_DETACH\n- 1: DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH  \n- 3: DLL_THREAD_DETACH\n- 0x100: Used in version calculation (256)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CallStaticInitializers: Runs C++ global constructors\n- ExitWithCleanup: Runs atexit handlers and destructors",
