      "name": "InvertBitBuffer",
      "signature": "void InvertBitBuffer(byte * pbSrc, byte * pbDst, int nBitLen)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Inverts (bitwise NOT) a source buffer into a destination buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate byte count from bit length: (nBitLen + 7) / 8\n2. Calculate aligned dword count: byteCount / 4\n3. Process 4-byte chunks in a loop, inverting each dword\n4. Handle remaining 1-3 bytes individually with fall-through\n\nParameters:\n- pbSrc (byte*): Source buffer to read from\n- pbDst (byte*): Destination buffer for inverted data\n- nBitLen (int): Length in bits to process\n\nReturns:\n- void",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
