      "name": "ScaleDoubleByExponent",
      "signature": "double ScaleDoubleByExponent(double dMantissa, short nExponent)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "double",
      "comment": "Scales a double by applying a new exponent value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract sign and mantissa bits from input double\n2. Add bias (0x3FE) to exponent and shift into position\n3. Combine mantissa bits with new exponent field\n4. Return reconstructed double\n\nParameters:\n- dMantissa (double): Normalized mantissa value (0.5 <= |m| < 1.0)\n- nExponent (short): Exponent value to apply\n\nReturns:\n- double: dMantissa * 2^nExponent\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3FE (1022): IEEE 754 double exponent bias minus 1\n- 0x800F: Mask preserving sign bit and lower mantissa bits\n- 0x10: Shift factor for exponent field alignment",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:96ef86ea161c5c47c2f79058ef6d533b",
