      "name": "ReadBitsFromBuffer",
      "signature": "dword ReadBitsFromBuffer(dword * pBitBuffer, int nBitCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Reads specified number of bits from a bit buffer and returns the value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate requested bits won't exceed buffer capacity\n2. Loop reading up to 8 bits per iteration from current byte\n3. Apply upper bit mask to extract bits at current offset\n4. Shift and accumulate into result value\n5. Advance byte pointer when crossing byte boundary\n\nParameters:\n- pBitBuffer (dword*): Bit buffer structure [pCurByte, nTotalBits, nByteIdx, nBitOffset]\n- nBitCount (int): Number of bits to read (1-32)\n\nReturns:\n- Extracted bit value as dword\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8: Bits per byte boundary check\n- g_abUpperBitMasks: Per-offset masks to extract upper N bits from byte\n- g_adwBitMasks: Masks for extracting N bits (0,1,3,7,15,31,63,127,255)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:9878c3132e3616bb6cb52a5bd878cec3",
