      "name": "ConvertDateTimeToTimestamp",
      "signature": "int ConvertDateTimeToTimestamp(int nYear, int nMonth, int nDay, int nHour, int nMinute, int nSecond, int nDstStatus)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts date/time components to Unix-style timestamp.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate year is in range 1970-2038 (0x76c-0x76c+0x8a)\n2. Calculate day-of-year from month cumulative days table + day\n3. Add leap day if year divisible by 4 and month > February\n4. Compute total days since epoch with leap year correction\n5. Convert to seconds: ((hours + days*24)*60 + minutes)*60 + seconds\n6. Add timezone offset and DST adjustment if applicable\n\nParameters:\n- nYear (int): Year (1970-2038)\n- nMonth (int): Month (1-12)\n- nDay (int): Day of month\n- nHour (int): Hour (0-23)\n- nMinute (int): Minute (0-59)\n- nSecond (int): Second (0-59)\n- nDstStatus (int): DST mode: 1=apply, -1=auto-detect, 0=none\n\nReturns:\n- Unix timestamp (seconds since epoch), or -1 if year out of range\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x76c (1900): Base year subtracted to get year offset\n- 0x46 (70): Minimum valid year offset (1970)\n- 0x8a (138): Maximum valid year offset (2038)\n- 0x16d (365): Days per non-leap year\n- 0x18 (24): Hours per day\n- 0x3c (60): Minutes per hour / seconds per minute\n- 0x7c558180: Epoch adjustment constant",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
