      "name": "FormatDoubleExponential",
      "signature": "char * FormatDoubleExponential(double * pdValue, char * szBuffer, int nPrecision, int nCapital)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Formats a double value as exponential notation string (e.g., \"1.234e+005\").\n\nCalled from __cfltcvt when format is 'e' (0x65) or 'E' (0x45).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Decompose double into mantissa/exponent via FUN_6ff799e8\n2. Check sign: nDigitInfo[0] == 0x2d ('-') indicates negative\n3. Round mantissa to precision+1 digits via FUN_6ff79971\n4. Build final string with sign, decimal point, exponent via FUN_6ff7397b\n\nParameters:\n- pdValue (double*): Pointer to double value to format\n- szBuffer (char*): Output buffer for formatted string\n- nPrecision (int): Number of digits after decimal point\n- nCapital (int): Non-zero to use 'E', zero for 'e'\n\nReturns:\n- szBuffer pointer for chaining",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
