      "name": "AtomicRead64",
      "signature": "void AtomicRead64(longlong * pllOutput, longlong * pllSource)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Atomically reads a 64-bit value using CMPXCHG8B instruction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load comparand from EBX:ECX (implicit __fastcall registers)\n2. Execute LOCK CMPXCHG8B to atomically read [pllSource]\n3. Store result (EDX:EAX) to pllOutput\n\nParameters:\n- pllOutput (longlong*): Destination for the read 64-bit value\n- pllSource (longlong*): Source memory location to read atomically\n- IMPLICIT: EBX contains low dword of comparand (typically 0)\n\nReturns:\n- void (result stored in pllOutput)\n\nNotes:\n- CMPXCHG8B always loads the original value into EDX:EAX\n- The comparison/swap aspect is unused; this exploits the atomic read side-effect\n- Used by GetUptimeSeconds to safely read g_qwInitTimestamp",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:9d6cfcfa33002e2999cc90a8d4912760",
