      "name": "DestroyCriticalSectionArray",
      "signature": "void DestroyCriticalSectionArray(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Destroys all dynamically allocated critical sections in the global array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through critical section array from 0x6ff83d6c to 0x6ff83e2c\n2. Skip NULL entries and reserved critical sections (g_pCritSect1-4)\n3. For non-reserved entries: DeleteCriticalSection then MemFree\n4. Finally destroy the 4 reserved critical sections\n\nParameters:\n- None (uses global array g_apCritSectArray)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6ff83d6c: Start of critical section pointer array\n- 0x6ff83e2c: End of array (48 entries, 0xC0 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n- void",
