      "name": "OpenFileWithFlags",
      "signature": "int OpenFileWithFlags(LPCSTR lpszFilePath, uint dwOpenFlags, uint dwShareMode, uint dwPermFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Opens a file using CreateFileA and returns a CRT file descriptor.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SECURITY_ATTRIBUTES based on O_NOINHERIT flag (0x80)\n2. Set text mode flag (0x80) if not binary and not unicode mode\n3. Map open flags (param_2 & 3) to Windows GENERIC_READ/WRITE\n4. Map share mode (param_3) to FILE_SHARE_* flags\n5. Map creation mode (param_2 & 0x700) to CREATE_* disposition\n6. Build CreateFileA attributes from flag bits\n7. Allocate a file descriptor from the CRT table\n8. Call CreateFileA and verify file type\n9. For append mode on text files, seek to check for Ctrl-Z marker\n\nParameters:\n- lpszFilePath (LPCSTR): Path to file to open\n- dwOpenFlags (uint): CRT-style open flags (_O_RDONLY, _O_WRONLY, etc.)\n- dwShareMode (uint): Share mode (0x10=none, 0x20=read, 0x30=write, 0x40=r+w)\n- dwPermFlags (uint): Permission flags for file creation\n\nReturns:\n- File descriptor (0+) on success\n- -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) on failure, sets errno\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x80: O_NOINHERIT flag / FILE_ATTRIBUTE_NORMAL\n- 0x8000: O_BINARY flag\n- 0x4000: O_TEXT flag\n- 0x16: EINVAL errno value\n- 0x18: EMFILE errno value (too many files)\n- 0x1a: Ctrl-Z (EOF marker for text mode)\n- 0x24: Size of file descriptor table entry (36 bytes)",
