      "name": "GetExecutableDirectory",
      "signature": "bool GetExecutableDirectory(LPSTR szPathOut, dword dwBufSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Gets the directory path of the current executable module.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output buffer with null terminator\n2. Call GetModuleFileNameA(NULL) to get current module path\n3. Calculate string length using REPNE SCASB\n4. Search backward for path separator ('\\\\', '/', ':')\n5. Truncate at separator to get directory only\n\nParameters:\n- szPathOut (LPSTR): Output buffer for directory path\n- dwBufSize (dword): Size of output buffer in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- 1 (true): Directory path extracted successfully\n- 0 (false): GetModuleFileNameA failed or no separator found\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x5C (92): Backslash path separator '\\\\'\n- 0x2F (47): Forward slash path separator '/'\n- 0x3A (58): Colon drive separator ':'",
