      "name": "GetStringTypeWithConversion",
      "signature": "BOOL GetStringTypeWithConversion(DWORD dwInfoType, char * lpszSrcStr, int nSrcLen, WORD * pwCharType, UINT nCodePage, LCID dwLocaleId, int nUseFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "BOOL",
      "comment": "Retrieves character type information for a string with codepage conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If API mode not determined (g_nStringTypeApiMode=0), probe Unicode/ANSI support\n2. Try GetStringTypeW with empty string - if succeeds, mode=1 (Unicode)\n3. Else try GetStringTypeA - if succeeds, mode=2 (ANSI only)\n4. If both fail, return FALSE\n5. If mode=2: Call GetStringTypeA directly with locale\n6. If mode=1: Convert multibyte to widechar via MultiByteToWideChar\n7. Call GetStringTypeW on converted widechar string\n\nParameters:\n- dwInfoType (DWORD): Character type info to retrieve (CT_CTYPE1/2/3)\n- lpszSrcStr (char*): Source multibyte string to analyze\n- nSrcLen (int): Length of source (-1 for null-terminated)\n- pwCharType (WORD*): Output buffer for character type info per char\n- nCodePage (UINT): Code page (0 uses g_nDefaultCodePage)\n- dwLocaleId (LCID): Locale ID for ANSI path (0 uses g_dwLocaleId)\n- nUseFlags (int): Non-zero enables MB_ERR_INVALID_CHARS (0x8)\n\nReturns:\n- TRUE on success with character types filled in pwCharType\n- FALSE on failure or if neither Unicode nor ANSI APIs available\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8: MB_ERR_INVALID_CHARS flag for MultiByteToWideChar\n- 1: Unicode API mode (GetStringTypeW available)\n- 2: ANSI-only API mode (GetStringTypeA only)",
