      "name": "BuildHuffmanDecodeTables",
      "signature": "int BuildHuffmanDecodeTables(byte * pbBitLengths)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Builds Huffman decoding tables from an array of bit lengths.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Zero-initialize bit length counts array (16 entries for codes 0-15)\n2. Count occurrences of each bit length in input, validating lengths < 16\n3. Compute prefix sum offsets for symbol sorting\n4. Sort symbols by bit length into temporary buffer\n5. Copy sorted bit lengths to g_abBitLengthCopy\n6. Build code tracking array g_abCodeTrack with incremental codes\n7. Build decode table entries:\n   - Short codes (<=8 bits): Direct table entry with symbol and length\n   - Long codes (>8 bits): Two-level table with secondary lookup\n\nParameters:\n- pbBitLengths (byte*): Array of 256 bit lengths (0-15), one per symbol\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success (all 256 symbols processed)\n- 0 on failure (null byte or invalid length encountered early)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10 (16): Maximum bit length count array size\n- 0x100 (256): Number of symbols to process\n- 0xff (255): Loop limit for symbol iteration\n- 8: Threshold between short/long Huffman codes",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
