      "name": "ConvertHexCharToValue",
      "signature": "uint ConvertHexCharToValue(uint dwChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Converts hex character to numeric value for format parsing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if character is decimal digit (0-9) using ctype version\n2. If g_dwCTypeVersion < 2: lookup in g_pbCharTypeTable\n3. Else: call TestCharacterTypeMask with digit mask\n4. If NOT a digit (hex letter A-F/a-f):\n   - Clear case bit (0xDF) to normalize case\n   - Subtract 7 to map A->10, B->11, etc.\n5. Return converted value\n\nParameters:\n- dwChar (uint): ASCII character code to convert\n\nReturns:\n- For digits 0-9: Returns dwChar unchanged\n- For hex letters: Returns case-normalized value in 0x3A-0x3F range\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xFFFFFFDF: Case-clearing mask (clears bit 5)\n- 7: Maps 'A' (0x41) to 0x3A (caller subtracts '0' later)\n- 4: Digit character type mask in ctype table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:aee0add5b0bd27cdd12dfdccdafd8a6d",
