      "name": "ChangeFileSize",
      "signature": "int ChangeFileSize(uint nFileDesc, int nNewSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Changes file size by extending or truncating to nNewSize bytes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current file position via SeekFile(SEEK_CUR)\n2. Get current file end via SeekFile(SEEK_END)\n3. If nNewSize > current end: write zero-filled blocks to extend\n4. If nNewSize < current end: truncate via SetEndOfFile\n5. Restore original file position\n\nParameters:\n- nFileDesc (uint): CRT file descriptor\n- nNewSize (int): Target file size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success, -1 on failure (sets errno to EACCES=0xD)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1000 (4096): Block size for zero-fill writes\n- 0x8000: File mode flag passed to FUN_6ff7d867\n- 0xD (13): EACCES errno value\n- 5: ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED OS error code",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
