      "name": "AsciiDigitsTo96BitMantissa",
      "signature": "void AsciiDigitsTo96BitMantissa(char * szDigits, int nDigitCount, uint * pdwMantissa)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts ASCII digit string to 96-bit normalized floating-point mantissa.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 96-bit accumulator (pdwMantissa[0..2]) to zero\n2. For each digit: multiply accumulator by 10, add digit value\n3. Multiply by 10: shift left twice (*4), add original (*5), shift left (*10)\n4. Normalize: shift left 16 bits at a time while high word is zero\n5. Fine-normalize: shift left 1 bit at a time until MSB is set\n6. Store final exponent at pdwMantissa offset +10 (2-byte field)\n\nParameters:\n- szDigits (char*): Array of digit values (0-9, not ASCII chars)\n- nDigitCount (int): Number of digits to process\n- pdwMantissa (uint*): 12-byte buffer for 96-bit mantissa + 2-byte exponent\n\nReturns:\n- void: Output written to pdwMantissa buffer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x404e (16462): Initial exponent bias for 80-bit extended precision\n- 0xfff0 (-16): Exponent adjustment per 16-bit coarse shift\n- 0xffff (-1): Exponent adjustment per 1-bit fine shift\n- 0x8000: MSB mask for normalization check",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b41de5b81e6f5c290111b6d697b33467",
