      "name": "RegisterAtExitCallback",
      "signature": "dword RegisterAtExitCallback(dword pfnCallback)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Registers a callback function in the atexit table for cleanup at process exit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Lock exit handler mutex\n2. Check if table has space (compare current size vs available)\n3. If full, reallocate table with 16 additional bytes (4 entries)\n4. Store callback pointer at g_pAtExitTableEnd\n5. Increment end pointer by 4 bytes\n6. Unlock mutex and return\n\nParameters:\n- pfnCallback (dword): Function pointer to register for exit cleanup\n\nReturns:\n- Non-zero (callback value) on success\n- 0 on allocation failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10 (16): Bytes to grow table (4 new entries)\n- 0x4 (4): Entry stride (sizeof function pointer)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
