      "name": "AllocateSbhRegion",
      "signature": "void * AllocateSbhRegion(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates a new Small Block Heap (SBH) region entry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If region array is full, expand it by 16 entries via HeapReAlloc\n2. Get pointer to next available entry slot (0x14 byte structure)\n3. Allocate header memory (0x41c4 bytes) via HeapAlloc with HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY\n4. Allocate virtual memory region (1MB) via VirtualAlloc with MEM_RESERVE\n5. Initialize entry fields and increment region count\n6. On any allocation failure, clean up and return NULL\n\nParameters:\n- None (uses global SBH state)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to new SBH region entry on success\n- NULL on allocation failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14 (20): SBH region entry structure size (5 DWORDs)\n- 0x41c4 (16836): SBH header allocation size\n- 0x100000 (1MB): Virtual memory region size\n- 0x2000: MEM_RESERVE flag\n- 8: HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b59a8a7d2c8fdcc2aac183f01f99a847",
