      "name": "SetFileHandle",
      "signature": "int SetFileHandle(uint dwFileDesc, HANDLE hFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Sets a Windows handle in the file descriptor table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dwFileDesc is within range (< g_dwMaxFileDesc)\n2. Calculate table offset: (dwFileDesc & 0x1F) * 0x24\n3. Check slot is empty (handle == -1)\n4. For stdin/stdout/stderr (0/1/2), also update Windows standard handles\n5. Store hFile in the descriptor table slot\n6. On failure, set errno=EBADF (9) and return -1\n\nParameters:\n- dwFileDesc (uint): File descriptor number (0-2 are std streams)\n- hFile (HANDLE): Windows handle to store\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success, -1 on failure (invalid fd or slot in use)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24 (36): File descriptor entry stride in table\n- 0x1F: Mask for entry index within table block\n- 0xFFFFFFF6 (-10): STD_INPUT_HANDLE\n- 0xFFFFFFF5 (-11): STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE\n- 0xFFFFFFF4 (-12): STD_ERROR_HANDLE\n- 9: EBADF (Bad file descriptor errno)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
