      "name": "InitCodePageCharTypeTable",
      "signature": "int InitCodePageCharTypeTable(int nCodePageId)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes the character type table for a given code page.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Lock critical section 0x19 for thread safety\n2. Resolve special code page IDs (-2=OEM, -3=ACP, -4=default) via ResolveSpecialCodePage\n3. If already cached for this code page, return success immediately\n4. Search known code page table (g_adwKnownCodePages) for predefined entries\n5. If found in table, populate g_abCharTypeTable from predefined byte ranges\n6. If not found, call GetCPInfo and build char type table from lead byte ranges\n7. For multi-byte code pages, mark lead bytes with 0x4 and all bytes with 0x8\n8. Update globals: cached code page, multi-byte flag, locale ID, data fields\n9. Call FUN_6ff7c500 to finalize character case mapping tables\n\nParameters:\n- nCodePageId (int): Code page identifier or special value (-2, -3, -4)\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success\n- -1 on failure (GetCPInfo failed and not special code page)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x19: Critical section index for code page subsystem\n- 0x30 (48): Stride of known code page table entries\n- 0x40 (64): DWORDs to clear in char type table (257 bytes total)\n- 0x4: Lead byte marker in char type table\n- 0x8: Multi-byte valid marker in char type table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
