      "name": "ShiftStringRight",
      "signature": "void ShiftStringRight(char * szBuffer, int nShiftOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Shifts a string right in-place to create space for insertion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nShiftOffset is zero, return immediately\n2. Get string length (including null terminator)\n3. Move entire string right by nShiftOffset bytes using MoveMemory\n\nParameters:\n- szBuffer (char*): String buffer to shift (must have space for shift)\n- nShiftOffset (int): Number of bytes to shift right\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nNotes:\n- Buffer must have sufficient space for string + shift offset\n- Handles overlapping memory via MoveMemory\n- Caller responsible for filling gap at start of buffer",
