      "name": "FindHashTableEntryById",
      "signature": "void * FindHashTableEntryById(FogHashTable * pHashTable, int nKeyId)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Searches hash table for entry matching the given key ID.\nIterates through all buckets with critical section synchronization.\nReturns pointer to found entry or NULL if not found.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return NULL if bucket count is zero (empty table)\n2. For each bucket index from 0 to bucketCount:\n   a. Enter critical section for this bucket via Ordinal_10050\n   b. Walk linked list at bucket head\n   c. For each entry, compare ID at +0x10 with nKeyId\n   d. If match found, leave critical section and return entry\n   e. Otherwise leave critical section and try next bucket\n3. Return NULL if not found after all buckets exhausted\n\nParameters:\n- pHashTable (FogHashTable*): Hash table structure pointer\n  +0x08: bucket count (uint)\n  +0x14: pointer to bucket heads array\n  +0x1c: pointer to critical section array (0x18 stride)\n- nKeyId (int): Key ID to search for (compared at entry+0x10)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to matching entry, or NULL (0) if not found\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x18 (24): CRITICAL_SECTION stride per bucket\n- 0x10 (16): Entry key ID field offset\n- 0x04 (4): Entry next pointer field offset",
