      "name": "ComputeExtendedRemainder",
      "signature": "float10 ComputeExtendedRemainder(float10 * __return_storage_ptr__)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "float10 *",
      "comment": "Computes IEEE remainder of two extended precision floats.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check divisor (ST1) exponent for valid range (mask 0x7FFF0000)\n2. If exponent valid, delegate to ComputeExtendedRemainderInternal\n3. If divisor mantissa is non-zero, scale both operands by 2^64 and retry\n4. Otherwise compute simple remainder via FPREM instruction\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: ST0 contains dividend\n- IMPLICIT: ST1 contains divisor\n\nReturns:\n- float10 remainder in ST0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7FFF0000: Exponent mask for 80-bit extended float\n- 0x7FBE: Exponent threshold for scaling path\n- g_dScaleFactor2Pow64: Scaling constant (2^64 as double)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ba64e7d70c2bcd8b3838963a89363cf4",
