      "name": "MoveMemory",
      "signature": "void * MoveMemory(void * pDest, void * pSrc, uint dwBytes)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Copies dwBytes from pSrc to pDest, correctly handling overlapping memory regions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check for overlap: if pDest > pSrc && pDest < pSrc + dwBytes\n2. If overlapping, copy backward from end to avoid corruption\n3. Handle alignment: align destination to 4-byte boundary first\n4. Copy DWORDs in unrolled loop (8 DWORDs per iteration) when count >= 8\n5. Copy remaining 0-7 DWORDs via switch fallthrough\n6. Copy remaining 0-3 bytes individually\n\nParameters:\n- pDest (void*): Destination buffer\n- pSrc (void*): Source buffer\n- dwBytes (uint): Number of bytes to copy\n\nReturns:\n- Original pDest pointer (for chaining)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3: Alignment mask (check low 2 bits)\n- 0x8: DWORD threshold for unrolled loop\n- 0x4: Bytes per DWORD",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
