      "name": "LCMapStringWithConversion",
      "signature": "int LCMapStringWithConversion(LCID dwLocaleId, uint dwMapFlags, char * szSrcStr, int nSrcLen, LPWSTR pwszDest, int nDestLen, UINT nCodePage, int nMultiByte)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Maps characters using locale-aware case conversion with codepage conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SEH frame for exception handling\n2. Check g_nLCMapMode to determine Unicode support:\n   - If 0: Test LCMapStringW, set mode to 1 (Unicode) or 2 (ANSI)\n3. If positive nSrcLen, compute actual length via FUN_6ff7db45\n4. If mode=2 (ANSI-only): Call LCMapStringA directly and return\n5. If mode=1 (Unicode):\n   a. Get required wide-char buffer size via MultiByteToWideChar\n   b. Allocate stack buffer via AllocaStackProbe\n   c. Convert source to wide-char\n   d. Call LCMapStringW to perform mapping\n   e. If not LCMAP_SORTKEY: Convert result back via WideCharToMultiByte\n6. Restore SEH and return result\n\nParameters:\n- dwLocaleId (LCID): Locale identifier for mapping rules\n- dwMapFlags (uint): LCMap flags (LCMAP_LOWERCASE=0x100, LCMAP_UPPERCASE=0x200)\n- szSrcStr (char*): Source ANSI string to map\n- nSrcLen (int): Source length in bytes (-1 for null-terminated)\n- pwszDest (LPWSTR): Destination buffer or NULL for size query\n- nDestLen (int): Destination buffer size in characters\n- nCodePage (UINT): Code page for conversion (0 uses g_nDefaultCodePage)\n- nMultiByte (int): If non-zero, use MB_ERR_INVALID_CHARS flag\n\nReturns:\n- Character count written on success\n- 0 on failure or when querying required size with NULL dest\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x100: LCMAP_LOWERCASE\n- 0x200: LCMAP_UPPERCASE\n- 0x400: LCMAP_SORTKEY (returns sort key, not mapped string)\n- 0x220: WC_NO_BEST_FIT_CHARS | WC_COMPOSITECHECK\n- 0x8: MB_ERR_INVALID_CHARS",
