      "name": "InvalidateFileDescriptor",
      "signature": "int InvalidateFileDescriptor(uint dwFileDesc)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Invalidates a file descriptor by clearing its handle in the file table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate file descriptor is within max range\n2. Calculate table index (param>>5) and entry offset (param&0x1F)*0x24\n3. Check entry is open (flag bit 0 set) and has valid handle (!= -1)\n4. For stdin/stdout/stderr (0/1/2), call SetStdHandle(NULL) to disconnect\n5. Set handle to -1 (invalidated)\n6. On invalid descriptor, set errno=EBADF(9) and return -1\n\nParameters:\n- dwFileDesc (uint): File descriptor index to invalidate\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success\n- -1 on failure (invalid/closed descriptor, sets errno=EBADF)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24 (36): File entry structure stride\n- 0x1F (31): Mask for entry index within table block\n- 0xFFFFFFF6 (-10): STD_INPUT_HANDLE\n- 0xFFFFFFF5 (-11): STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE  \n- 0xFFFFFFF4 (-12): STD_ERROR_HANDLE\n- 9: EBADF errno value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:c2bda2cc0331ae5bf6246d61a0224d72",
