      "name": "CleanupHeapAllocations",
      "signature": "void CleanupHeapAllocations(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Releases all heap memory based on heap mode during CRT shutdown.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If heap mode 3 (virtual alloc): iterate entries, VirtualFree each allocation, HeapFree metadata\n2. If heap mode 2 (linked list): traverse circular list, VirtualFree each node's allocation\n3. Destroy process heap via HeapDestroy\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3: Heap mode using VirtualAlloc with entry array\n- 0x2: Heap mode using circular linked list\n- 0x4000: MEM_DECOMMIT flag for VirtualFree\n- 0x8000: MEM_RELEASE flag for VirtualFree\n- 0x100000: 1MB region size to decommit\n- 0x14 (20): Stride of heap entry structure (5 DWORDs)\n- 0xC (12): Offset to VirtualAlloc pointer in entry\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CRTDllMain: Calls this during DLL_PROCESS_DETACH",
