      "name": "ComputeSha1Hash",
      "signature": "void ComputeSha1Hash(uint * pdwHashOut, byte * pbData, uint dwDataLen)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Computes SHA-1 hash of input data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 5-word state with SHA-1 magic constants (H0-H4)\n2. Process input in 64-byte (0x40) blocks:\n   a. Copy block to message schedule W[0-15]\n   b. Expand W[16-79] via XOR and left-rotate by 1\n   c. Run 80 rounds in 4 groups of 20 each:\n      - Round 0-19: F=(B AND C) OR ((NOT B) AND D), K=0x5A827999\n      - Round 20-39: F=B XOR C XOR D, K=0x6ED9EBA1\n      - Round 40-59: F=(B AND C) OR (B AND D) OR (C AND D), K=0x8F1BBCDC\n      - Round 60-79: F=B XOR C XOR D, K=0xCA62C1D6\n   d. Add working variables back to state\n3. Copy final 5-word state (20 bytes) to output buffer\n\nParameters:\n- pdwHashOut (uint*): Output buffer for 20-byte (5-word) SHA-1 hash\n- pbData (byte*): Input data buffer to hash\n- dwDataLen (uint): Length of input data in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x67452301, 0xEFCDAB89, 0x98BADCFE, 0x10325476, 0xC3D2E1F0: SHA-1 initial H0-H4\n- 0x5A827999: Round 0-19 constant (sqrt(2) * 2^30)\n- 0x6ED9EBA1: Round 20-39 constant (sqrt(3) * 2^30)\n- 0x8F1BBCDC: Round 40-59 constant (sqrt(5) * 2^30)\n- 0xCA62C1D6: Round 60-79 constant (sqrt(10) * 2^30)\n- 0x40 (64): SHA-1 block size in bytes\n- 0x14 (20): Rounds per group, also hash output size in bytes",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
