      "name": "ConvertWideCharToMultiByteSafe",
      "signature": "int ConvertWideCharToMultiByteSafe(char * szOutBuf, ushort wChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Thread-safe wrapper for wide character to multibyte conversion.\nEnsures locale state is consistent during character conversion operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment g_nLocaleRefCount for thread-safe reference tracking\n2. Check g_fLocaleLocked flag for exclusive locale lock state\n3. If locked: decrement ref count, acquire critical section 0x13\n4. Call ConvertWideCharToMultiByteSingle for actual WideCharToMultiByte\n5. If was locked: release critical section\n6. Else: decrement locale reference count\n7. Return conversion result\n\nParameters:\n- szOutBuf (char*): Output buffer for multibyte character (minimum 4 bytes)\n- wChar (ushort): Wide character to convert\n\nReturns:\n- Positive: Number of bytes written to output buffer\n- -1: Conversion error (errno set to 0x2A / EDOM)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x13: Critical section index for locale operations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
