      "name": "WriteFileNoLock",
      "signature": "int WriteFileNoLock(dword nFileDesc, byte * pbBuffer, dword nBytesToWrite)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Writes buffer to file handle without locking (internal CRT function).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return 0 immediately if nBytesToWrite is 0\n2. Calculate file table entry from descriptor (entry = g_apFileTable[fd>>5] + (fd&0x1f)*0x24)\n3. If FAPPEND flag (0x20) set, seek to end of file first\n4. If text mode flag (0x80) set:\n   a. Copy bytes to temp buffer, converting LF to CRLF\n   b. Write in chunks of 0x400 bytes max\n   c. Track newline count to adjust return value\n5. If binary mode: call WriteFile directly with original buffer\n6. On success: return bytes written minus newline count (logical bytes)\n7. On error: set errno/oserror and return -1\n8. Special: if FDEV flag (0x40) set and first byte is 0x1A (EOF), return 0\n\nParameters:\n- nFileDesc (dword): CRT file descriptor index\n- pbBuffer (byte*): Source buffer to write\n- nBytesToWrite (dword): Number of bytes to write\n\nReturns:\n- Logical bytes written (adjusted for CRLF expansion) on success\n- 0 if nBytesToWrite is 0 or EOF marker on device\n- -1 on error (sets errno)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24 (36): File entry structure stride\n- 0x20: FAPPEND flag (seek to end before write)\n- 0x80: FTEXT flag (text mode, do CRLF conversion)\n- 0x40: FDEV flag (device/character mode)\n- 0x400 (1024): Text mode chunk buffer size\n- 0x1A (26): DOS EOF character (Ctrl+Z)\n- ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED (5): Maps to EBADF (9)",
