      "name": "AllocateLogMessage",
      "signature": "int * AllocateLogMessage(void * this, int nInsertMode, int nMessageLen, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Allocates a LogMessage structure and optionally links it into a doubly-linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_401 (SMemAlloc) with size = nMessageLen + 0x40, ORing dwFlags with 0x8\n2. If allocation succeeds, initialize pNext and pPrev fields to 0\n3. If nInsertMode == 0, return allocated node without linking\n4. If node is already linked, unlink from current position first\n5. If nInsertMode == 1, insert at tail of list\n6. If nInsertMode != 1, insert at head of list\n7. Update list head/tail pointers as needed\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: this (ECX) = LogManager instance (pListHead at +0x4, dwTailOffset at +0x8)\n- nInsertMode (int): 0=allocate only, 1=insert at tail, other=insert at head\n- nMessageLen (int): Message payload size (final allocation is +0x40 larger)\n- dwFlags (uint): Memory allocation flags (ORed with 0x8)\n\nReturns:\n- int*: Pointer to allocated LogMessage structure, or NULL on failure\n\nStructure Layout (LogMessage):\n- +0x00: pNext (pointer to next node)\n- +0x04: pPrev (offset or ~pointer to previous location)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
