      "name": "ToLowerCaseLocaleAware",
      "signature": "uint ToLowerCaseLocaleAware(void * this, uint dwChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Converts a character to lowercase using locale-aware mapping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If no locale set (g_dwLocaleId == 0), simple ASCII conversion: A-Z \u2192 a-z\n2. For single-byte chars (< 0x100), check if uppercase via ctype table\n3. If not uppercase, return unchanged\n4. For multi-byte chars, swap byte order based on lead byte flag\n5. Call LCMapString wrapper with LCMAP_LOWERCASE (0x100) flag\n6. Extract result based on returned byte count (1 or 2 bytes)\n\nParameters:\n- this (void*): Unused __thiscall context\n- nChar (uint): Character code to convert (can be multi-byte)\n\nReturns:\n- Lowercase character code, or original if no mapping exists\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x41-0x5A (65-90): ASCII 'A'-'Z' range\n- 0x20 (32): Offset to convert ASCII upper to lower\n- 0x100 (256): Single-byte/multi-byte boundary; also LCMAP_LOWERCASE flag\n- 0x80: Lead byte indicator flag in ctype table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:cc0e19248bdb90cb6bf790db102f9ddf",
