      "name": "ConvertStringToLong",
      "signature": "long ConvertStringToLong(byte * pbString, byte * * ppbEndPtr, int nBase, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "long",
      "comment": "Converts a string to a long integer with configurable base and flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Skip leading whitespace (character mask 0x8)\n2. Parse optional sign ('+' or '-'), set flag bit 1 if negative\n3. Validate base (0-36, but 1 is invalid)\n4. Auto-detect base if 0: \"0x\"/\"0X\" = hex(16), \"0\" = octal(8), else decimal(10)\n5. Skip \"0x\"/\"0X\" prefix for explicit base 16\n6. Parse digits: 0-9 as values 0-9, A-Z/a-z as values 10-35\n7. Accumulate result checking for overflow via max quotient pre-calculation\n8. On overflow, set errno to ERANGE (0x22) and clamp to limits\n\nParameters:\n- pbString (byte*): Input string to parse\n- ppbEndPtr (byte**): Receives pointer to first unparsed char (or original if none parsed)\n- nBase (int): Radix 2-36 (0=auto-detect, 1=invalid)\n- dwFlags (uint): Control flags: bit0=unsigned mode, bit1=negative sign, bit2=overflow, bit3=valid digit parsed\n\nReturns:\n- Parsed long value (negated if signed), 0 if no valid digits, clamped on overflow\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2d (45): '-' ASCII\n- 0x2b (43): '+' ASCII\n- 0x30 (48): '0' ASCII\n- 0x78/0x58: 'x'/'X' ASCII\n- 0x37 (55): Offset to convert A-F to values 10-15\n- 0x24 (36): Maximum valid base\n- 0x22 (34): ERANGE errno value\n- 0x7fffffff: INT_MAX\n- 0x80000000: INT_MIN boundary",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
