      "name": "TriggerFpuExceptions",
      "signature": "void TriggerFpuExceptions(byte byExceptMask)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Triggers specific FPU exceptions to clear corresponding exception flags in the status word.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test bit 0x01 (Invalid): Load extended double, convert to int (FISTP)\n2. Test bit 0x08 (Overflow): Store extended double as double, save FPU status\n3. Test bit 0x10 (Underflow): Store denormalized extended double as double\n4. Test bit 0x04 (Zero Divide): Compute 1.0/0.0 via FDIVRP\n5. Test bit 0x20 (Inexact): Load PI and store as double (loses precision)\n\nParameters:\n- byExceptMask (byte): Bitmask of exception types to trigger\n  0x01=Invalid, 0x04=ZeroDiv, 0x08=Overflow, 0x10=Underflow, 0x20=Inexact\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6ff86350: Extended double constant for Invalid/Overflow operations\n- 0x6ff8635c: Denormalized extended double for Underflow operation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d2372372c4179c2cdb1a710877220f60",
