      "name": "ConvertDoubleToExtended",
      "signature": "void ConvertDoubleToExtended(uint * pExtOut, uint * pDoubleIn)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts IEEE 754 double (64-bit) to 80-bit extended precision format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract sign bit (bit 63), exponent (bits 62-52), mantissa (bits 51-0)\n2. Handle special cases:\n   - Zero: Returns zero extended format\n   - Denormalized (exp=0): Adjust exponent and normalize\n   - Infinity/NaN (exp=0x7FF): Map to extended exp 0x7FFF\n   - Normal: Bias convert (add 0x3C00 to exponent)\n3. Shift mantissa left 11 bits, set implicit bit\n4. Normalize denormals by left-shifting until MSB is set\n\nParameters:\n- pExtOut (uint*): Output 10-byte extended precision buffer\n- pDoubleIn (uint*): Input 8-byte double precision value\n\nReturns:\n- void: Result written to pExtOut as 10-byte extended format\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7FF (2047): Double max exponent (infinity/NaN)\n- 0x7FFF (32767): Extended max exponent\n- 0x3C00 (15360): Exponent bias adjustment (16383-1023)\n- 0x80000000: Implicit mantissa bit for normalized numbers",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d7ddf3c1b7f31503b888765ebbb66d57",
