      "name": "TestCharacterTypeMask",
      "signature": "uint TestCharacterTypeMask(int nCharCode, uint dwTypeMask)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Tests if a character matches specified character type flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For single-byte characters (< 0x100), look up type in g_pbCharTypeTable directly\n2. For multi-byte characters, check if lead byte has 0x80 flag (DBCS indicator)\n3. If DBCS, build 2-byte sequence; else build 1-byte sequence\n4. Call GetStringTypeA/W to get character type for multi-byte sequence\n5. Return type flags masked by dwTypeMask\n\nParameters:\n- nCharCode (int): Character code to test (single or multi-byte)\n- dwTypeMask (uint): Bitmask of character types to test (e.g., CT_CTYPE1)\n\nReturns:\n- Non-zero if character matches any requested type flags\n- 0 if character type lookup fails or no flags match\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x100 (256): ASCII range boundary for direct table lookup\n- 0x80: DBCS lead byte indicator flag in character type table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
