      "name": "SbhAllocFromNodes",
      "signature": "void * SbhAllocFromNodes(uint dwBlockSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates a block from the Small Block Heap (SBH) node pool.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Start at g_pSbhCurrentNode and iterate through circular node list\n2. For each node with valid arena (offset != -1), search free slots\n3. Check slots from current position to end of descriptor array\n4. Then check slots from beginning up to current position\n5. If slot has enough space, call sub-allocator to carve out block\n6. If no nodes have space, search sentinel list for uncommitted pages\n7. Allocate virtual memory for new pages via VirtualAlloc\n8. Initialize page headers and free lists, then allocate from new page\n9. If sentinel exhausted, call AllocHeapArena for new arena\n\nParameters:\n- dwBlockSize (uint): Size of block in allocation units (not bytes)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated block on success, NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2018 (8216): End of descriptor array in node (0x806 DWORDs)\n- 0x1000 (4096): Page size\n- 0xF0 (240): Initial free space in page\n- 0xF1 (241): Marker for maximum allocation size\n- 0x10 (16): Maximum pages to allocate at once\n- 0x100 (256): Offset from page base to user data\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6ff76248: Sub-allocator that carves blocks from pages\n- AllocHeapArena: Creates new arena when all nodes exhausted",
