      "name": "ClassifyExponentParity",
      "signature": "uint ClassifyExponentParity(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Classifies a floating-point exponent from ST0 by integer parity.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare ST0 with ROUND(ST0) to check if integer\n2. If not integer, return 0\n3. If integer, multiply by 0.5 and check if result is integer\n4. Return 2 if even integer, 1 if odd integer\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: ST0 contains the exponent value to classify\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Non-integer exponent\n- 1: Odd integer exponent\n- 2: Even integer exponent\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ComputePowerExponentiation (caller)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
