      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts string to long integer using base 10.\n\nWrapper function that calls ConvertStringToLong with base=10 and flags=0.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Pass input string to ConvertStringToLong\n2. Use base 0xa (decimal) for conversion\n3. Use flags=0 for standard conversion behavior\n4. Return the converted integer value\n\nParameters:\n- this (void*): Object context pointer (ECX, __thiscall convention)\n- szInput (char*): Input string to parse for integer value\n- ppEndPtr (char**): Output pointer to first invalid char, NULL to ignore\n- pReserved (void*): Reserved parameter, passed through to inner function\n\nReturns:\n- Parsed integer value from string (base 10)\n- 0 if no valid digits found or input is empty\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ConvertStringToLong: Full string-to-long parser with base and flags",
