      "name": "SetFpuControlWordBits",
      "signature": "short SetFpuControlWordBits(ushort wMask, ushort wBits)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "short",
      "comment": "Sets specific bits in the FPU control word while preserving others.\n\nUses the formula: newCtrlWord = (wBits & wMask) | (~wMask & oldCtrlWord)\nThis allows selectively modifying only the bits specified by the mask.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store current FPU control word to stack via FSTCW\n2. Compute masked bits: (wBits & wMask)\n3. Compute preserved bits: (~wMask & oldCtrlWord)\n4. OR results to form new control word\n5. Load new control word via FLDCW\n6. Return old control word (sign-extended to int)\n\nParameters:\n- wMask (ushort): Bit mask specifying which bits to modify\n- wBits (ushort): New values for the masked bit positions\n\nReturns:\n- Old FPU control word value before modification",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
