      "name": "ReadFileWithTextMode",
      "signature": "int ReadFileWithTextMode(uint dwFileHandle, byte * pbBuffer, uint dwBytesToRead)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Read from file with CR-LF to LF text mode conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate buffer pointer is not NULL\n2. Look up file entry in g_apFileTable using handle (slot = handle >> 5, offset = (handle & 0x1f) * 0x24)\n3. Check if file is not in EOF state (flag 0x02)\n4. If unbuffered text mode (0x48) and pushback char exists, consume it first\n5. Call ReadFile to read raw bytes\n6. On error: ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED(5) sets errno=EBADF(9), ERROR_BROKEN_PIPE(0x6d) returns 0, else map error\n7. If text mode (0x80 flag), process CR-LF conversion:\n   - CR-LF pair becomes single LF\n   - Ctrl-Z (0x1a) marks EOF\n   - Lone CR at buffer end: peek next byte with 1-byte read\n\nParameters:\n- dwFileHandle (uint): File handle (encodes table slot and entry index)\n- pbBuffer (byte*): Output buffer for read data\n- dwBytesToRead (uint): Max bytes to read\n\nReturns:\n- Bytes read on success (after CR-LF conversion)\n- 0 on EOF or broken pipe\n- -1 on error\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24 (36): File table entry stride\n- 0x02: EOF flag\n- 0x04: CR seen flag\n- 0x40: Binary mode flag\n- 0x48: Unbuffered text with pushback\n- 0x80: Text mode flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
