      "name": "GetHeapBlockSize",
      "signature": "dword GetHeapBlockSize(void * pMemBlock)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Returns the size of a heap memory block from the appropriate heap manager.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up SEH frame for exception handling\n2. If g_dwHeapMode == 3 (small block heap):\n   a. Lock critical section 9\n   b. Find small block entry for pMemBlock\n   c. If found, size = *(pMemBlock-4) - 9 (stored size minus header)\n   d. Unlock small block heap\n3. If g_dwHeapMode == 2 (virtual heap):\n   a. Lock critical section 9\n   b. Find virtual heap block entry\n   c. If found, size = first byte << 4 (page count * 16)\n   d. Unlock virtual heap\n4. If block not found in custom heaps, call HeapSize on process heap\n5. Restore SEH frame and return size\n\nParameters:\n- pMemBlock (void*): Pointer to allocated memory block\n\nReturns:\n- Block size in bytes on success\n- SIZE_T from HeapSize if not in custom heaps\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3: Small block heap mode\n- 0x2: Virtual heap mode\n- 0x9: Critical section index for heap locks\n- -4: Offset to size field in small block header\n- 9: Small block header overhead to subtract\n- 4: Shift count for virtual block page-to-byte conversion",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:eef5ae1e69543f2ca247fd0a568bf7f0",
