      "name": "ClearBitsFromPosAndRound",
      "signature": "uint ClearBitsFromPosAndRound(uint * pdwBitArray, int nBitPos)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Clears bits from position to end of 96-bit array with rounding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if bit at nBitPos is set\n2. If set AND all lower bits are zero, propagate carry (round up)\n3. Clear all bits from nBitPos onwards using mask\n4. Zero remaining DWORDs after the current one\n\nParameters:\n- pdwBitArray (uint*): Pointer to 96-bit array (3 DWORDs)\n- nBitPos (int): Bit position to clear from (0-95)\n\nReturns:\n- Non-zero if carry was propagated, 0 otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Bits per DWORD\n- 0x1f (31): Bit index mask\n- 3: Total DWORDs in 96-bit array",
