      "name": "ComputePowerFromFPU",
      "signature": "void ComputePowerFromFPU(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Wrapper to compute power (x^y) from FPU stack registers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x10 bytes stack space for two doubles\n2. FXCH swaps ST0 and ST1 (exponent now in ST0)\n3. Store ST1 (base) to [ESP] as double\n4. Store ST0 (exponent) to [ESP+0x8] as double\n5. Call pow helper with stack-based double arguments\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: ST0 contains exponent value\n- IMPLICIT: ST1 contains base value\n\nReturns:\n- void (result returned via FPU stack by callee)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GenerateGammaTable: Sole caller, uses for gamma power computation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f4e79a9374712478a96f5f0af7ec0c2f",
