      "name": "CloseFileDescriptor",
      "signature": "int CloseFileDescriptor(uint dwFileDesc)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Closes a file descriptor after validating it.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dwFileDesc < g_dwMaxFileDesc\n2. Check file entry flag bit 0 is set (file in use)\n3. If valid: lock file entry via FUN_6ff7bcea\n4. Close the underlying handle via CloseFileDescriptorHandle\n5. Unlock file entry via FUN_6ff7bd49\n6. If invalid: set errno to EBADF(9), oserr to 0\n\nParameters:\n- dwFileDesc (uint): CRT file descriptor index\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success\n- -1 on error (invalid descriptor sets errno=EBADF)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24 (36): FileEntry structure stride\n- 0x1f (31): Mask for entry index within table segment\n- 9: EBADF error code (bad file descriptor)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
