      "name": "GetFPUStatusWord",
      "signature": "int GetFPUStatusWord(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Retrieves the current FPU (Floating Point Unit) status word.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up stack frame\n2. Execute FSTSW instruction to store FPU status word to stack\n3. Sign-extend the 16-bit status word to 32-bit int via MOVSX\n4. Clean up stack frame and return\n\nParameters:\n- None (reads directly from FPU hardware)\n\nReturns:\n- FPU status word as signed int containing:\n  - Exception flags (bits 0-5): invalid, denormal, zero-div, overflow, underflow, precision\n  - Stack fault (bit 6), error summary (bit 7)\n  - Condition codes (bits 8,9,10,14): C0-C3\n  - Top of stack pointer (bits 11-13)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
