      "name": "FreeTreeNodeRecursive",
      "signature": "void FreeTreeNodeRecursive(StringIndexNode * pNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Recursively frees all nodes in a binary tree using post-order traversal.\nThis ensures child nodes are freed before their parent.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If left child (pNode->pLeft at offset 0x24) exists, recurse on it\n2. If right child (pNode->pRight at offset 0x28) exists, recurse on it  \n3. Free the current node via FreePoolMemoryTracked(0, pNode)\n\nParameters:\n- pNode (StringIndexNode*): Pointer to tree node to free recursively\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nStructure Layout (StringIndexNode):\n- 0x24: pLeft - left child pointer\n- 0x28: pRight - right child pointer\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FreeIndexTree: Entry point that initiates tree destruction",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:fa12eaa84afc8286ba7e060aab7434e5",
