      "name": "TriggerStackDump",
      "signature": "void TriggerStackDump(HANDLE hThread)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Triggers a stack dump on the specified thread for debugging.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check registry for stack dump disabled setting via Ordinal_423\n2. Validate ImageHelp loaded, event handle, and thread handle exist\n3. Duplicate target thread handle (or current thread if NULL)\n4. Signal stack walk event to wake the stack walker thread\n5. Lower target thread priority to THREAD_PRIORITY_IDLE (-15)\n6. Wait indefinitely for stack walk completion event\n7. Restore original thread priority and cleanup\n\nParameters:\n- hThread (HANDLE): Thread to dump stack for (NULL = current thread)\n\nReturns:\n- void (logs errors via Ordinal_10030)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7FFFFFFF (THREAD_PRIORITY_ERROR_RETURN): Invalid priority sentinel\n- -0xF (-15): THREAD_PRIORITY_IDLE\n- 0xFFFFFFFF (INFINITE): Wait timeout value\n- 2 (DUPLICATE_SAME_ACCESS): DuplicateHandle options",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
