      "name": "CreateListenSocket",
      "signature": "SOCKET CreateListenSocket(int nQueueServer, ushort wPort)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "SOCKET",
      "comment": "Creates a TCP listening socket for the queue server on the specified port.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create I/O completion port for async operations\n2. Create TCP socket (AF_INET, SOCK_STREAM)\n3. Set socket options: TCP_NODELAY and SO_KEEPALIVE\n4. Set socket to non-blocking mode via ioctlsocket\n5. Bind socket to specified port on any interface\n6. Start listening with backlog of 250 connections\n7. Store socket/port/IOCP handles in server structure arrays\n8. Spawn accept thread (LAB_6ff66e40) for incoming connections\n9. Optionally spawn additional worker thread (LAB_6ff67510) if enabled\n\nParameters:\n- pQueueServer (int): Pointer to queue server structure (cast as int)\n- wPort (ushort): Port number to listen on\n\nReturns:\n- SOCKET handle on success, 0 on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xB8C: Port count offset in server structure\n- 0xB90: Socket array offset (SOCKET[4])\n- 0xBA0: Port array offset (ushort[8])\n- 0xBA8: Port active flags array offset\n- 0xBD8: Accept thread handles array offset\n- 0xBE8: Accept thread IDs array offset\n- 0xC08: IOCP handles array offset\n- 0xC18: Secondary thread enable flag offset\n- 0xC1C: Worker thread handles array offset\n- 0xC2C: Worker thread IDs array offset\n- 0xFA (250): Listen backlog size",
