      "name": "DumpThreadContext",
      "signature": "void DumpThreadContext(HANDLE hThread)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Dumps thread context and memory regions for debugging.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Logs debug header via Ordinal_10030\n2. Zeroes out CONTEXT structure (0xB3 dwords = 716 bytes)\n3. Sets ContextFlags to CONTEXT_FULL (0x10007)\n4. Retrieves thread context via GetThreadContext\n5. Logs 0x1000 bytes around ESP (stack region)\n6. Logs 0x20 bytes around EIP (code region)\n7. Triggers full stack dump via TriggerStackDump\n8. Calls Ordinal_10040 for cleanup/finalization\n\nParameters:\n- hThread (HANDLE): Handle to target thread\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xB3 (179): CONTEXT size in DWORDs (716 bytes)\n- 0x10007: CONTEXT_FULL flag\n- 0x1000: Stack dump size (4KB)\n- 0x20: Code dump size (32 bytes)",
