      "name": "FormatFloatExponential",
      "signature": "char * FormatFloatExponential(char * szBuffer, int nPrecision, int nUpperCase, int * pnDecimalInfo, char chPadFlag)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Formats floating-point number in scientific/exponential notation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If chPadFlag set, call ShiftStringRight to make room for sign/decimal\n2. Check if number is negative (0x2d at pnDecimalInfo[0])\n3. Write '-' sign if negative, advance write position\n4. Move first digit before decimal, insert locale decimal separator\n5. Copy exponent template \"e+000\" via string copy helper\n6. Replace 'e' with 'E' (0x45) if nUpperCase non-zero\n7. Calculate actual exponent from pnDecimalInfo[1] - 1\n8. If exponent negative, write '-' sign and negate value\n9. Fill in hundreds, tens, ones digits of exponent by modifying template\n\nParameters:\n- szBuffer (char*): Output buffer for formatted string\n- nPrecision (int): Number of decimal digits to include\n- nUpperCase (int): Non-zero uses 'E', zero uses 'e'\n- pnDecimalInfo (int*): Decimal info structure:\n  [0]=sign (0x2d if negative), [1]=exponent+1, [3]=digit string ptr\n- chPadFlag (char): Non-zero to shift buffer for insertion\n\nReturns:\n- szBuffer (char*): Pointer to formatted output string\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2d (45): ASCII '-' minus sign\n- 0x45 (69): ASCII 'E' uppercase exponent marker\n- 99, 9: Thresholds for 3-digit and 2-digit exponent formatting",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:16032f476aba0e42e163f0f1660d4b55",
