      "name": "BeginClientRead",
      "signature": "BOOL BeginClientRead(void * pServer, uint * pClient, int nLogErrors)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "BOOL",
      "comment": "Initiates an asynchronous read on a client connection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter client critical section at offset 0x2c\n2. Calculate remaining buffer space (0x5b4 - current position)\n3. If buffer full, log error and disconnect client\n4. Verify read not already in progress (flag 0x4 at offset 0x58)\n5. Set read-in-progress flag\n6. If socket handle is INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE (-1), disconnect\n7. Increment client refcount before async operation\n8. Call ReadFile with overlapped I/O at offset 0x44\n9. Handle ERROR_IO_PENDING (0x3e5) as success\n10. On real error, log and disconnect client\n\nParameters:\n- pServer (void*): Server context\n- pClient (uint*): Client connection structure\n- nLogErrors (int): Non-zero to enable error logging\n\nReturns:\n- TRUE on successful read initiation or pending\n- FALSE on error or disconnect\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x5b4 (1460): Maximum buffer size\n- 0x90 (144): Read buffer offset in client struct\n- 0x3e5 (997): ERROR_IO_PENDING",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
