      "name": "DisconnectClientAndBlock",
      "signature": "void DisconnectClientAndBlock(void * pServer, uint dwClientId, uint dwReason, uint dwBlockDuration)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Disconnects a client from the server and adds their IP to the block cache.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if server not initialized (offset 0xbd0 == 0)\n2. Look up client entry by ID in hash table using mask at offset 0xc\n3. If client not found, log and return\n4. Log client IP address via inet_ntoa\n5. Re-lookup client, mark as disconnecting (offset 0xc = 1)\n6. Close socket via Ordinal_10000, set socket to INVALID_SOCKET (-1)\n7. Decrement reference count via InterlockedDecrement\n8. If refcount reaches 0, remove from both client ID and IP hash tables\n9. Call cleanup function FUN_6ff650e0 on client entry\n10. Add client IP to block cache with specified duration\n\nParameters:\n- pServer (void*): Server context structure\n- dwClientId (uint): Client identifier for hash table lookup\n- dwReason (uint): Disconnect reason code (passed to logging)\n- dwBlockDuration (uint): Duration to block IP (passed to AddIpToBlockCache)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xbd0: Server initialized flag offset\n- 0xc: Hash mask offset in server struct\n- 0x14: Client hash table pointer offset\n- 0x1c: Critical section array offset\n- 0x18: Hash bucket stride (24 bytes per bucket)\n- 0x854: Global critical section offset\n- 0x880: Active client count offset\n- 0xbc8: Callback function pointer offset",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:4db6d0b5f34902d3c119b6cc1b7804da",
