      "name": "PrintSystemInfo",
      "signature": "void PrintSystemInfo(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Prints system diagnostic information to debug output.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Prints separator line and current date/time\n2. Determines OS type from global flag and copies OS name string\n3. Prints OS version info with version number from global\n4. Calls PrintCpuInfo to output processor details\n5. Prints total physical memory in MB\n6. Gets and prints application path if available\n7. Gets and prints local IP address via Ordinal_10013\n8. Gets and prints computer name via GetComputerNameA\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x104 (260): MAX_PATH buffer size\n- 0x40 (64): Computer name buffer size\n\nGlobals:\n- g_nOsType: OS type flag (1=Win95, 2=Win98, 3=WinNT, 4=Win2000, 5=MacOS)\n- g_dwTotalPhysMemory: Total physical memory in bytes\n- g_flOsVersion: OS version number (float)",
