      "name": "ReportExceptionContext",
      "signature": "void ReportExceptionContext(int nExceptionCode, char * szSource, int nLine, char * szExpression)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Reports exception context for error handling and diagnostics.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if exception code is 10 (thread context) - save thread handle\n2. Call CheckExceptionReentrance to prevent nested exception handling\n3. If not reentrant, set g_fExceptionActive flag\n4. Call DisplayErrorMessageBox with error info\n5. Zero 0xB3 dwords of CONTEXT structure at g_threadContext\n6. Set context flags to 0x10007 (CONTEXT_FULL)\n7. If thread handle provided, call GetThreadContext\n8. Else capture current thread context via inline assembly trick\n9. For codes 2,5,6,7,10: log stack (0x1000 bytes) and code (0x20 bytes)\n10. Call optional callback g_dwFogParam2 if registered\n11. Format and flush log output\n12. Clear g_fExceptionActive unless code is 2,5,6 (persistent errors)\n\nParameters:\n- nExceptionCode (int): Error type (2=memory, 5=assert, 6=assert+handle, 7=warning, 10=thread)\n- szSource (char*): Source file string, or thread HANDLE when code=10\n- nLine (int): Source line number\n- szExpression (char*): Error message or assert expression\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10007: CONTEXT_FULL (control+integer+segments+debug regs)\n- 0xB3 (179): CONTEXT structure size in dwords (716 bytes)\n- 0x1000: Stack dump size (4KB)\n- 0x20: Code dump size (32 bytes)",
