      "name": "OutputDebugMessage",
      "signature": "uint OutputDebugMessage(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Formats and outputs debug messages based on flag bits in ECX.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x1014 bytes stack space for message buffer\n2. If flag 0x4 set, prepend timestamp (HH:MM:SS.mmm format) via GetLocalTime\n3. Append format string using FUN_6ff72fbe (snprintf-like)\n4. If flag 0x2 NOT set, output via OutputDebugStringA\n5. If flag 0x1 set, write to log file via FUN_6ff6ffc0\n6. If flags 0x18 set, check Caps Lock state via GetKeyState(0x14)\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: ECX contains output flags\n- IMPLICIT: EDX contains format string pointer\n- IMPLICIT: Stack+0x1018 contains varargs pointer\n\nReturns:\n- Result varies by code path (typically 0 or Caps Lock state)\n\nFlag Bits (ECX):\n- 0x01: Write to log file\n- 0x02: Suppress OutputDebugStringA\n- 0x04: Prepend timestamp\n- 0x18: Check Caps Lock state",
