      "name": "BuildModuleList",
      "signature": "int * BuildModuleList(dword dwProcessId)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Builds a sorted linked list of loaded modules for a process using Toolhelp32 APIs.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Attempts to load toolhelp32 functions from kernel32.dll or tlhelp32.dll\n2. Gets CreateToolhelp32Snapshot, Module32First, Module32Next function pointers\n3. Creates a module snapshot with TH32CS_SNAPMODULE flag (0x8)\n4. Iterates through modules, allocating 0x210 byte entries for each\n5. Copies module name (offset 0x0) and path (offset 0x104) into entry\n6. Stores module base address at offset 0x204, sorts entries by base address\n7. Builds linked list via pointer at offset 0x20c\n\nParameters:\n- dwProcessId (dword): Target process ID for module enumeration\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to head of sorted module list on success\n- NULL (0) on failure (library load or snapshot creation failed)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8: TH32CS_SNAPMODULE flag for CreateToolhelp32Snapshot\n- 0x210 (528): Size of module entry structure\n- 0x104 (260): MAX_PATH, offset to module path in entry\n- 0x204: Offset to module base address in entry\n- 0x20c: Offset to next pointer in entry (linked list)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6ff6e360 (caller): Uses module list for process analysis",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:830e00ebde3185a128193750cdc503ad",
