      "name": "SelectHeapType",
      "signature": "int SelectHeapType(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Determines which heap allocator type to use.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query OS version via GetVersionExA\n2. If Windows Server 2003+ (platform 2, major >= 5), return 1 (default heap)\n3. Otherwise, check __MSVCRT_HEAP_SELECT environment variable\n4. Parse env var format: module=heaptype,... with semicolon separators\n5. Convert module name to uppercase and compare to current module\n6. Return parsed heap type value (1, 2, or 3) from env var\n7. Fall back to FUN_6ff74f87 to determine type (returns 2 or 3)\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Default Windows heap\n- 2: Small-block heap\n- 3: Old heap allocator\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x94 (148): OSVERSIONINFOA structure size\n- 0x104 (260): MAX_PATH\n- 0x2c (44): ASCII comma delimiter\n- 0x3b (59): ASCII semicolon separator",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
