      "name": "ProcessCompletionPortEvents",
      "signature": "uint ProcessCompletionPortEvents(FogHashTable * pServer, int nChannelIdx, DWORD dwTimeout)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Processes I/O completion port events for a server channel.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Cache start time and loop for up to 100ms\n2. Call GetQueuedCompletionStatus on the channel's completion port\n3. Look up client by completion key via HashTableFindEntry\n4. Determine operation type from overlapped flags (bit 0=read, bits 0-1=2 for write)\n5. On read completion: update recv stats, process messages, requeue read\n6. On write completion: dequeue send buffer, send more if queued\n7. On error/zero bytes: disconnect client\n8. Release client reference and continue loop\n\nParameters:\n- pServer (FogHashTable*): Server context containing completion ports at offset 0xC08\n- nChannelIdx (int): Index into completion port array (0-3)\n- dwTimeout (DWORD): Initial wait timeout for GetQueuedCompletionStatus\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if any read operation was processed successfully\n- 0 if timeout or only write/error operations\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x64 (100): Maximum loop duration in milliseconds\n- 0x102: ERROR_TIMEOUT from GetLastError\n- 0x44: Offset from overlapped to client struct for read ops\n- 0x5C: Offset from overlapped to client struct for write ops\n- 0xC08: Offset to completion port handles array in server struct",
