      "name": "ParseFormatInput",
      "signature": "int ParseFormatInput(void * this, int * pnCharCount, byte * pbFormat, uint * * ppVarArgs)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Parses input according to scanf-style format specifiers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Skip leading whitespace in input stream\n2. For each format char, match literal or parse specifier:\n   - '%' starts format specifier parsing\n   - Handles width, size modifiers (h/l/L/I64/w)\n   - Supports: c, s, d, i, o, u, x, p, e, f, g, n, [charclass]\n3. Extract values from input and store to varargs destinations\n4. Track conversion count and character position\n\nParameters:\n- this (void*): Input stream object (ECX)\n- pnCharCount (int*): Format string pointer (reused as iterator)\n- pbFormat (byte*): Varargs pointer (advances per conversion)\n- ppVarArgs (uint**): Output destination pointer list\n\nReturns:\n- Number of successful conversions, -1 on EOF with no conversions\n\nSize Modifiers:\n- 'h': short (decrement cSizeMod)\n- 'l': long (increment cSizeMod)\n- 'L': long double (increment cSizeMod)\n- 'I64': 64-bit integer\n- 'w': wide character mode\n\nFormat Types (lowercase normalized):\n- 0x63 ('c'): character\n- 0x64 ('d'): signed decimal\n- 0x65-0x67 ('e'-'g'): floating point\n- 0x69 ('i'): signed integer (auto base)\n- 0x6e ('n'): store char count\n- 0x6f ('o'): octal\n- 0x70 ('p'): pointer\n- 0x73 ('s'): string\n- 0x75 ('u'): unsigned decimal\n- 0x78 ('x'): hexadecimal\n- 0x7b ('{'): character class scanset",
