      "name": "ProcessFormatSpecifier",
      "signature": "int ProcessFormatSpecifier(int * pOutState, byte * pbFormat, uint * * ppVarArgs)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Parses printf-style format string and outputs formatted text.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Parse format string character-by-character using state machine\n2. State 0: Output literal characters, handle lead bytes for MBCS\n3. State 1: Initialize format specifier on '%'\n4. State 2: Parse flag characters (-, +, 0, #, space)\n5. State 3: Parse width field (numeric or *)\n6. State 4-5: Parse precision field after '.'\n7. State 6: Parse size modifiers (h, l, I64, w)\n8. State 7: Execute format type (d/i/u/x/X/o/p/s/S/c/C/e/E/f/g/G/n/Z)\n\nParameters:\n- pOutState (int*): Output context pointer\n- pbFormat (byte*): Format string to parse\n- ppVarArgs (uint**): Pointer to va_list arguments\n\nReturns:\n- Number of characters output on success\n- Negative value on error\n\nFlag Bits (dwFlags):\n- 0x01: Show plus sign\n- 0x02: Space prefix for positive\n- 0x04: Left justify\n- 0x08: Zero pad\n- 0x10: Long size (l)\n- 0x20: Short size (h)\n- 0x40: Signed type\n- 0x80: Alternate form (#)\n- 0x100: Negative value\n- 0x200: Octal alternate\n- 0x800: Wide string (w)\n- 0x8000: 64-bit integer (I64)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
