      "name": "GetSaveDirectoryPath",
      "signature": "void GetSaveDirectoryPath(char * szPathOut, dword dwBufSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Retrieves and initializes the Diablo II save directory path.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Try reading \"Save Path\" registry value under \"Diablo II\" key\n2. If path invalid/missing, try \"InstallPath\" registry value\n3. If still invalid, derive path from module directory\n4. Append \"Save\\\" subdirectory and write to \"Save Path\" registry\n5. Ensure trailing backslash on final path\n6. Create directory recursively if it doesn't exist\n\nParameters:\n- szPathOut (char*): Output buffer for save directory path\n- dwBufSize (dword): Size of output buffer in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- void (path written to szPathOut, empty string on failure)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x5c (92): Backslash character '\\'\n- 0xffffffff: INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_422: Registry read string value\n- Ordinal_425: Registry write string value\n- CreateDirectoryRecursive: Ensures directory exists",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:c3908b01344b38a65d1f8bd1a2aee78f",
