      "name": "CreateStrPack",
      "signature": "void CreateStrPack(int * pStrPack, byte byMaxBits, char * szCharSet)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes a StrPack structure for character-to-index mapping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validates pStrPack pointer and non-empty szCharSet\n2. Zeros 0x204 bytes (0x81 dwords) of structure\n3. Iterates through szCharSet, assigning unique indices to each character\n4. Builds two lookup tables: char->index at offset 4, index->char at offset 0x103\n5. Calculates and stores minimum bit count needed for index range at offset 0\n\nParameters:\n- pStrPack (int*): Output structure, minimum 0x204 bytes\n- byMaxBits (byte): Maximum bits allowed (asserts if exceeded)\n- szCharSet (char*): Source character set string\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value. Structure initialized via pStrPack pointer.\n- Asserts on: NULL pStrPack, empty szCharSet, or index overflow\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x81 (129): DWORD count for zeroing (0x204 bytes total)\n- 0x4: Offset to char-to-index lookup table (256 entries)\n- 0x103: Offset to index-to-char reverse table\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FogAssert: Validation failures\n- ExitWithCode: Fatal exit on assertion",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:d231bcc7cb242ca4ab20206d4b353270",
