      "name": "InitAsyncData",
      "signature": "void InitAsyncData(int nEnable)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes async data subsystem with event array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert if async data already enabled (reinitialization error)\n2. Call Ordinal_284(0x40000) and Ordinal_285(0x4000) for buffer setup\n3. If nEnable is true:\n   a. Allocate 0x3000 bytes for event array (256 entries * 12 bytes)\n   b. Create 256 manual-reset events, storing HANDLE at offset 0\n   c. Initialize availability flag at offset 4 to 1\n   d. Set event count to 256 (0x100)\n   e. Set enabled flag to 1\n\nParameters:\n- nEnable (int): If non-zero, allocates and initializes event array\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nStructure Layout (12-byte stride):\n  +0x00: HANDLE hEvent (created via CreateEventA)\n  +0x04: int fAvailable (1 = available)\n  +0x08: (unused/padding)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3000 (12288): Array allocation size (256 * 12)\n- 0xC (12): Per-event structure stride\n- 0x100 (256): Total event count\n- 0x40000: Buffer size for Ordinal_284\n- 0x4000: Buffer size for Ordinal_285",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
