      "name": "SetAsyncDataPriority",
      "signature": "void SetAsyncDataPriority(void * pAsyncData, int nPriority)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets the priority of an async data operation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validates pAsyncData is non-NULL\n2. Verifies dwFlags signature (masked 0x41737960 = \"Asy`\")\n3. Validates nPriority is <= 0 (negative priorities only)\n4. If no pending ops (g_nAsyncPendingCount < 1):\n   - Updates priority directly and calls Ordinal_282\n5. If pending ops exist:\n   - If flag 0x8 not set: saves old priority, sets new, marks pending, links to list\n   - If flag 0x8 set: only updates if new priority is higher\n\nParameters:\n- pAsyncData (void*): Async data structure with fields at +0x3c, +0x44, +0x48, +0x4c, +0x50\n- nPriority (int): New priority value, must be <= 0\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x41737960: Async data signature (masked with 0xFFFFFFF0)\n- 0x8: Priority change pending flag\n- 0x44: Offset to current priority\n- 0x48: Offset to flags/signature\n- 0x4c: Offset to saved priority\n- 0x50: Offset to next pending link",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:ebf8263767f74d7cfbfaef530c13a3f3",
