      "name": "FogInit",
      "signature": "void FogInit(char * lpszGameName, uint dwParam2, char * lpszFilePath, bool fPrintSysInfo)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes the Fog library subsystems.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy game name and optional file path to globals\n2. If already initialized, optionally print system info and return\n3. Initialize critical sections and interlock system\n4. Set up memory pool and unhandled exception filter\n5. Validate gdwBitMasks/gdwInvBitMasks lookup tables\n6. Query OS version and set g_dwPlatformType enum\n7. Get physical memory size and system info\n8. Set g_fFogInitialized flag and complete init\n\nParameters:\n- lpszGameName (char*): Game name string (e.g. \"Diablo II\")\n- dwParam2 (uint): Stored to g_dwFogParam2\n- lpszFilePath (char*): Optional file path, copied to g_szFilePath\n- fPrintSysInfo (bool): If true, calls PrintSystemInfo\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x104 (260): MAX_PATH buffer size\n- 0x94 (148): sizeof(OSVERSIONINFOA)\n- 0x40000: Memory pool size\n- 0x8000: Memory pool reserve\n- 0x20 (32): Bit mask table size\n\nPlatform Types (g_dwPlatformType):\n- 0: Unknown/other\n- 1: Windows 95\n- 2: Windows 98/ME\n- 3: Windows NT\n- 4: Windows 2000/XP",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
